hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10801","10772 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated, my father narrated, from Rashid ibn Abi Najih, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith who said: I heard Ibn Abbas on this pulpit narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say these words in distress: There is no god but Allah, the Mighty, the Forbearing; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the mighty Throne; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and the earth, and Lord of the mighty Throne. Turn away from me the evil of so-and-so."
"10802","10773 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated, Hafs ibn Umar al-Kindi narrated, Salih ibn Hassan narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no harm in a man inspecting a slave-girl when he wants to buy her, except her private parts: what is between her knees and the knot of her waist-wrapper."
"10803","10774 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated, al-Mu'afa ibn Imran narrated, Musa ibn Khalaf al-Ammi narrated, from Abu al-Miqdam, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Jesus son of Maryam, peace be upon him, said: Matters are but three: a matter whose right guidance is clear to you, so follow it; a matter whose error is clear to you, so avoid it; and a matter disputed about, so refer it to one who knows it."
"10804","10775 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, Isa ibn Maymun narrated, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ka'b narrate, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the pulpit: Shall I not tell you of your worst? They said: Yes, if you wish, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Your worst is one who alights alone, flogs his slave, and withholds his help. He said: Shall I not tell you of worse than that? They said: Yes, if you wish, O Messenger of Allah. He said: One who hates people and whom they hate. He said: Shall I not tell you of worse than that? They said: Yes, if you wish, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Those who do not overlook a slip, nor accept an excuse, nor forgive a sin. He said: Shall I not tell you of worse than that? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: One whose good is not hoped for and whose evil is not safe from."
"10805","10776 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Masruq ibn al-Marzuban al-Kindi narrated, al-Musayyab ibn Sharik al-Amiri narrated, from Isa ibn Maymun, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Ibn Abbas, and from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from A'ishah, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and there were voices like the humming of bees reciting the Qur'an. He said: Islam shall spread, then it shall have a lull. Whoever's lull tends to excess and innovation, those are the people of the Fire."
"10806","10777 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated, from Isa ibn Maymun who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi narrate, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good character melts sins as water melts ice, and bad character corrupts deeds as vinegar corrupts honey."
"10807","10778 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated, and Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated, they said: Isa ibn Maymun narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two ravenous wolves spending the night among sheep are no more corrupting to them than the love of status and wealth is to the son of Adam."
"10808","10779 - al-Muntasir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Hadrami narrated, Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi al-Warraq narrated, Salih ibn Hassan narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you ask Allah, ask Him with the palms of your hands, and do not ask Him with their backs, and wipe your faces with them."
"10809","10780 - al-Muntasir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated, Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi narrated, from Salih ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything has a character, and the character of Islam is modesty."
"10810","10781 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated, Hisham ibn Ziyad Abu al-Miqdam narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything has an honor, and the honor of gatherings is what faces the qiblah. Whoever looks into his brother's writing without his permission, it is as if he looks into the Fire."
"10811","10782 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, from Ibn Abbas who said: Mut'ah existed at the start of Islam, and they used to read this verse: Then whatever you enjoy of them until a named term. A man would arrive in a town where he had no acquaintance and marry for as long as he thought he would need to finish his business, so that she would guard his goods and set his affairs right, until this verse was revealed: Forbidden to you are your mothers, to the end of the verse. The fixed term was abrogated and mut'ah was forbidden, and its confirmation in the Qur'an is: Except from their wives or what their right hands possess, for they are not blameworthy. Whatever is besides this private part is forbidden."
"10812","10783 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated, Za'idah narrated, Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to me, Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me, that Dhakwan, the chamberlain of A'ishah, narrated to him, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abbas came seeking permission to visit A'ishah. I came while at her head was her nephew Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr. I said: Here is Ibn Abbas seeking permission. Her nephew Abd Allah leaned over her and said: Here is Ibn Abbas seeking permission. She said: Leave me alone concerning Ibn Abbas, for I have no need of him. He said: O my mother, Ibn Abbas is among your righteous sons; he greets you and bids you farewell. She said: Admit him if you wish. I let him in, and when he sat he said: Rejoice. She said: Likewise. He said: Between you and joining Muhammad there is only the soul's leaving the body. You were the most beloved of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved only what was good. Your necklace fell on the night of al-Abwa', and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed till morning at the dwelling, and the people woke with no water with them, so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed that: Then seek clean earth. That was on your account and part of the concession Allah sent down for this community. And Allah the Exalted sent down your innocence from above seven heavens; the Trustworthy Spirit brought it, and there is no mosque of Allah's mosques in which Allah is remembered but it is recited therein night and day. She said: Leave me alone, O Ibn Abbas; by Him in whose hand is my soul, I wish I had been forgotten, forgotten."
"10813","10784 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Qariz ibn Shaybah, from Abu Ghatafan, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sniff water twice, and the ears are part of the head."
"10814","10785 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf and Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, they said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated, Isma'il ibn Umayyah narrated to me, that he heard Abu Ghatafan ibn Tarif al-Murri say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted the day of Ashura and commanded its fast. They said: O Messenger of Allah, a day venerated by Jews and Christians. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When next year comes, Allah willing, we shall fast the ninth. The next year did not come before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away."
"10815","10786 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiy narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated, Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated, Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind narrated, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Health and free time are two blessings in which many people are cheated."
"10816","10787 - Abu Yazid narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim narrated, Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever Allah wants good for, He gives him understanding in religion."
"10817","10788 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids, in the first rak'ah the Opening of the Book and: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and in the last the Opening of the Book and: Has there come to you the story of the Overwhelming."
"10818","10789 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated, and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Uthman ibn Muslim narrated, Wuhayb narrated, and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Umar ibn Ali narrated, and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Jarir narrated, and Abu Husayn al-Qadi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, they said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Uthman al-Harrani narrated, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, all of them from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder then prayed without touching water; the wording is that of the hadith of Yahya al-Qattan."
"10819","10790 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Abdan narrated to us, they said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Isma'il ibn Ulayyah narrated, from Ayyub, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder and did not perform ablution."
"10820","10791 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he had performed ablution, then he went out to prayer and was brought a tray with meat and bread, and he ate from it without performing ablution."
"10821","10792 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiy narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, who said: I entered the house of Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and found Abd Allah ibn Abbas there. We discussed ablution from what fire has touched, and Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to eat of what fire had touched, then pray without performing ablution. We said: Did you see him yourself? He pointed to his eyes and said: My eyes saw."
"10822","10793 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated, Wuhayb narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate from a shoulder, then prayed without performing ablution."
"10823","10794 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Junadah ibn Salm narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Amr, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat a shoulder or a foreleg, then lead the people in prayer without performing ablution."
"10824","10795 - Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid al-Baghdadi and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated, Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated, from Ayyub ibn Utbah, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Ibn Abbas who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the Farewell Hajj; he was brought a bone with meat while circumambulating the House on the day of Sacrifice, bit into it, then prayed without performing ablution."
"10825","10796 - Ja'far ibn Ahmad al-Sami al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Abu Usamah narrated, from al-Walid ibn Kathir who said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata narrated to me, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to prayer and met a gift, a limb of sheep, and ate a morsel or two from it, then prayed without performing ablution."
"10826","10797 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10827","10798 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats any of these greens of yours, let him not approach our mosque, for the angels are offended by what the sons of Adam are offended by."
"10828","10799 - Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, who heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah was washed in his shirt, and there descended into his grave Ali, al-Fadl ibn Abbas, Salih ibn Abbas, and Salih ibn Shuqran, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10829","10800 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated, Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, that he heard Ibn Abbas say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated on his mount during the Farewell Hajj, and touched the Corner with his crooked staff, out of dislike of pushing people away from it."
"10830","10801 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salm al-Razi narrated, Sa'id ibn Salim al-Qaddah narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated during the Farewell Hajj on his she-camel al-Qaswa'."
"10831","10802 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Malik al-Dabbi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Salih ibn Mismar narrated, Hisham ibn Sulayman narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, Salih ibn Abi Salih narrated to me, that he heard Ibn Abbas say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a woman afflicted with madness and said: Which is dearer to you: to be cured of this, or to endure and have Paradise? She said: Paradise is mine."
"10832","10803 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, and Ali narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated, both from Dawud ibn Qays, from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, that he heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha, in Madinah without fear or rain. He said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Why do you think he did that? He said: He wanted to make things easy for his community."
"10833","10804 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated, al-Nu'man ibn Abd al-Salam narrated, from Sufyan, from Dawud ibn Qays, from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10834","10805 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Adam narrated, and Muhammad ibn Abdus narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated, they said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated, from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, that Umm al-Fadl sent milk to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he drank while addressing the people at Arafah."
"10835","10806 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Nasa'i al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated, Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti narrated, Ziyad ibn Sa'd narrated, from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, from Ibn Abbas, that he saw no harm in a money-belt for one in ihram. And Ibn Abbas narrated that from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10836","10807 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Ishaq al-Jawhari narrated, Abu Asim narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, Ziyad informed me, that Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, informed him, that he heard Ibn Abbas narrate, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The womb has a hook holding to the waist of the Most Merciful; it joins whoever joins it and cuts whoever cuts it."
"10837","10808 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to change the religion of Ibrahim, peace be upon him, was Amr ibn Luhayy ibn Qama'ah ibn Khindif, father of Khuza'ah."
"10838","10809 - al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Talhah ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf, who said: I prayed with Ibn Abbas over a funeral, and he recited the Opening of the Book. I spoke to him about it, and he said: It is part of the Sunnah."
"10839","10810 - Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Huwayrith, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died at sixty-five, Abu Bakr at the same age as him, Umar ibn al-Khattab at fifty-six, and Uthman at eighty-one."
"10840","10811 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Nu'aym al-Wasiti narrated, Hushaym narrated, al-Madini narrated to me, from Abu al-Huwayrith, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the land is fertile, travel moderately and give the mounts their due, for Allah the Exalted is Gentle and loves gentleness. When it is barren, press on, and keep to night travel, for the earth is folded up at night. Beware of halting on the road itself, for it is the haunt of snakes and the track of beasts."
"10841","10812 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Nu'aym al-Wasiti narrated, Hushaym narrated, al-Madini narrated, from Abu al-Huwayrith, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing of the fornication of the people of the Jahiliyyah produced me; I was produced only by marriage like the marriage of Islam. Abu al-Qasim said: Al-Madini is in my view Fulayh ibn Sulayman."
"10842","10813 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Shayban narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Umar ibn Mu'attib, that Abu Hasan, freedman of Banu Nawfal, informed him, that he sought Ibn Abbas's fatwa about a slave who had a slave-woman under him and divorced her twice, then both were freed afterwards: is it lawful for the man to propose to her? Ibn Abbas said: Yes; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged to that effect."
"10843","10814 - Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Umar ibn Mu'attib, from al-Hasan, freedman of Banu Nawfal, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a slave who divorced a woman twice, then both were freed: may he marry her? He said: Yes. It was said: On whose authority? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave fatwa to that effect."
"10844","10815 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Umar ibn Mu'attib, that Abu Hasan, freedman of Banu Nawfal, informed him, that he sought Ibn Abbas's fatwa about a slave man who had a slave-woman under him and divorced her twice so she became separated, then both were freed afterwards: is it lawful for the man to propose to her? Ibn Abbas said: Yes; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged to that effect."
"10845","10816 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Umar ibn Uthman, nephew of Ali ibn Asim, narrated, Abu Tumaylah Yahya ibn Wadih narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Ma'bad, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two rak'ahs before dawn, in the first rak'ah the Opening of the Book and two verses from the end of al-Baqarah: The Messenger believes in what was sent down to him from his Lord, and in the second rak'ah the Opening of the Book and a verse of Al Imran: Say, O People of the Book, come to a word common between us and you, to the end of the verse."
"10846","10817 - al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, they said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated, from al-Qasim ibn Abbas, from Abd Allah ibn Umayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I live, Allah willing, till next year, I shall fast the ninth, fearing lest the day of Ashura escape me."
"10847","10818 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Hisham ibn Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Kinanah, from his father, who said: An amir among the amirs sent me to Ibn Abbas to ask him about istisqa'. He said: Who sent you? I said: So-and-so. He said: What kept him from coming to me to ask me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out humble, supplicating, in worn clothes; he did not deliver a sermon like this sermon of yours, and he prayed two rak'ahs as he prays in Eid."
"10848","10819 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, Isma'il ibn Rabi'ah ibn Hisham ibn Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Kinanah of Banu Amir ibn Lu'ayy narrated, that he heard his grandfather Hisham ibn Ishaq ibn Abd Allah narrate, from his father Ishaq ibn Abd Allah, that al-Walid ibn Utbah sent him to Abd Allah ibn Abbas saying: O son of my brother, ask him how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) acted in istisqa' on the day he sought rain with the people. Ishaq said: I entered upon Ibn Abbas and said: O Abu Abbas, how did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) act in istisqa' on the day he sought rain with the people? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out submissive and in worn clothes, and did therein as he did in Fitr and Adha."
"10849","10820 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated, Jarir narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah, from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a Jewish man and a Jewish woman who had been married, and they asked him to judge stoning for them, so he stoned them in the courtyard of the mosque."
"10850","10821 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had, from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, from Ya'qub ibn Khalid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Ablution is once each."
"10851","10822 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Na'im Abu Abd Allah, freedman of Umm Salamah, narrated to him, that he heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah saw a donkey branded on the face and disapproved of that. The man said: By Allah, I shall brand only at the farthest part from the face. He ordered a donkey of his to be branded on its buttocks."
"10852","10823 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, Hammam narrated, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, that he prayed behind Ibn Abbas over a funeral and he recited the Opening of the Book aloud. He said: I wanted people to know, and you to know, that it is the Sunnah."
"10853","10824 - Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated, my father narrated to me, Sabiq al-Jazari narrated, that Amr ibn Abi Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, informed him, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters. Whoever falls into them is likely to sin, and whoever avoids them safeguards his religion more, like one grazing beside a sanctuary about to fall into it. Every king has a sanctuary, and Allah's sanctuary is what He has made unlawful."
"10854","10825 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani narrated, Ibrahim ibn al-Mukhtar narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Harith ibn Fudayl, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyrs are on Bariq, a river at the gate of Paradise; their provision comes out to them morning and evening."
"10855","10826 - Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas al-Misri narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Salim Abu al-Nadr narrated to him, from Ziyad, freedman of Ibn Ayyash, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Uthman ibn Maz'un on the day he died, bent over him as if confiding to him, then raised his head and they saw traces of weeping in his eyes, then bent over him a second time, raised his head and they saw him weeping, then bent over him a third time, raised his head with a sob, and they knew he had died. The people wept, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hush; this is only from Satan, so seek Allah's forgiveness. Then he said: Go from you, O Abu al-Sa'ib, for you departed without becoming soiled with anything of it."
"10856","10827 - Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Abu al-Nadr narrated to him, from Ziyad, freedman of Ibn Ayyash, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the day Sa'd ibn Mu'adh was buried, while sitting at his grave, said: Had anyone been saved from the trial of the grave, Sa'd ibn Mu'adh would have been saved; he was squeezed once, then it was eased from him."
"10857","10828 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' narrated, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, Yazid ibn Hurmuz informed me, that Najdah al-Haruri, when he performed Hajj during the fitnah of Ibn al-Zubayr, sent to Ibn Abbas asking him about the share of the near relatives, for whom he deemed it. Ibn Abbas said: It is for the near relatives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10858","10829 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' narrated, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Numayri narrated, from Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli who said: I heard al-Zuhri narrate, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz, that Najdah al-Haruri, when he performed Hajj during the fitnah of Ibn al-Zubayr, sent to Ibn Abbas asking him about the share of the near relatives, saying for whom he deemed it. Ibn Abbas said: It is for the near relatives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided it among them. Umar had offered us something of it which we deemed less than our right, so we returned it to him and refused to accept it. He had offered them to help their marrying ones, pay off their debtors, and give to their poor, and refused to give them more than that."
"10859","10830 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, and Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated, they said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated, Qays ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz who said: I heard Ibn Abbas, when the letter of Najdah reached him, in which he wrote asking him about the near relatives mentioned by Allah in the Qur'an, about killing the children of polytheists and whether the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kill them, about when the orphanhood of an orphan ends, and about a slave and a woman present at battle. He said: Were it not to turn him back from an evil I fear he may fall into, I would not have written to him. He wrote about the near relatives: We used to deem the kin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to be them, but our people denied us that. As for the orphan, when he reaches marriageable age and sound judgment is perceived in him, his property is handed to him and his orphanhood has ended. As for children, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not kill the children of polytheists; you too, do not kill them, unless you know about them what al-Khidr knew of the boy when he killed him. About the slave and the woman, whether they have a share when they witness battle: he wrote to him that they have no fixed share, except to be given something from the spoils of the people."
"10860","10831 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated, from Za'idah, from al-A'mash, from al-Mukhtar ibn Sayfi, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz, who said: Najdah wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about an orphan, when orphanhood ends for him, about killing children, about a slave whether he has anything of the fay', and about the khums, for whom it is. Ibn Abbas said: Were it not that a folly might come from him, I would not have written to him. Then he wrote to him: As for the orphan, when he attains puberty and sound judgment is perceived in him, orphanhood has ended for him. As for children, if you know about them what al-Khidr knew, otherwise do not kill them. As for the slave, something used to be allotted to him. As for women, they used to treat the wounded and give water. As for the khums, we claim it is ours, while our people claim it is not ours."
"10861","10832 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated, and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, both from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz who said: Najdah wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about the khums, for whom it is, about a slave and a woman present at the spoils, whether they have anything of it, about the orphan, when the name of orphanhood is lifted from him, and about killing children. Ibn Abbas said: Were I not hoping Allah would benefit him by my letter, I would not have written to him. Then he said: Write, O Yazid: As for the khums, we used to deem it ours, but our people denied us that. As for the slave and the woman present at the spoils, they have nothing of it, but something is granted them. As for the orphan, orphanhood is lifted from him when he reaches puberty, and he becomes among the poor of the Muslims. As for children, do not kill them until you know about them what al-Khidr knew of the boy before he killed him; the wording is that of the hadith of Abu Ishaq al-Fazari."
"10862","10833 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz, that Najdah wrote to Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, asking him about five matters. Ibn Abbas said: Were it not that I would be concealing knowledge, I would not have written to him. Najdah wrote to him: Tell me, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) campaign with women? Did he strike a share for them? Did he kill children? When does an orphan's orphanhood end? And the khums, for whom is it? Ibn Abbas wrote to him: You wrote asking me: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) campaign with women? He did campaign with them; they treated the wounded and were granted something from the spoils, but as for a fixed share, he did not strike one for them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not kill children. You wrote: When does an orphan's orphanhood end? By my life, a man may grow a beard while still weak in looking after himself and weak in giving thereof; when he takes for himself in the soundest way people take, orphanhood has gone from him. You wrote asking me about the khums, for whom it is: We say it is ours, but our people denied us that."
"10863","10834 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz, that Najdah wrote to Ibn Abbas, and he mentioned the like of it."
"10864","10835 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated, Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali and al-Zuhri narrated to me, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Jarir narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz who said: Najdah wrote to Ibn Abbas, then he mentioned the hadith in words like those of Ja'far ibn Muhammad."
"10865","10836 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated, they said: Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated, Shurahbil ibn Sa'd al-Ansari narrated, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one for whom two daughters live on, to whom he does good as long as they accompany him and he accompanies them, except that they shall admit him into Paradise."
"10866","10837 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Mis'ar, from Abu Awn, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Wine was forbidden in itself, and intoxicants from every drink."
"10867","10838 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Mansur and al-A'mash, from Dharr, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I speak to myself about the matter of the Lord; to be reduced to charcoal is dearer to me than to utter it. Shu'bah said: One of them said: Praise be to Allah who could manage from you only whispering. And the other said: Praise be to Allah who turned his affair back to whispering."
"10868","10839 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, they said: Mis'ar narrated, from Abu Awn, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Wine was forbidden in itself, little and much of it, and intoxication from every drink."
"10869","10840 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Awn, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn Abbas, the like of it. This Abu Salamah is Mis'ar."
"10870","10841 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, Sharik narrated, from al-Abbas ibn Dharih, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn Abbas who said: Wine in itself is forbidden, little and much of it, and intoxication from every drink."
"10871","10842 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated, Sharik narrated, from Ayyash al-Amiri, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the prohibition of wine came down they said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not sell it? He said: The One who forbade its drinking forbade its sale."
"10872","10843 - al-Abbas al-Asfati narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Mindal ibn Ali narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or keep silent."
"10873","10844 - Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, Shayban narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no emigration after the Conquest, but jihad and intention; and when you are called to march forth, march forth."
"10874","10845 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud Sandilah narrated, Ibrahim ibn Ayyub al-Firsani narrated, Abu Hani' Isma'il ibn Khalifah narrated, from Ma'mar, from Za'idah, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever conceals knowledge he knows shall be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire. He said: It is testimony held by a man who is called to it or not called to it, while he knows it, and does not guide its owner to it; that is this knowledge."
"10875","10846 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prescribed punishments shall not be carried out in mosques, nor shall a father be retaliated against for a son."
"10876","Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Umar ibn Hawshab informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas: that three divorces used to be counted as one at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10877","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, (Ha), and Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, both saying: Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed in blind turmoil or in stone-throwing fighting among them with a stone or a whip or a stick, his blood-money is the blood-money of accidental killing, and whoever kills deliberately, then retaliation for his hand; so whoever stands between him and him, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither repentance nor ransom will be accepted from them."
"10878","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"10879","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"10880","Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashii al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: We, the company of the prophets, were commanded to hasten the breaking of the fast, and to delay the pre-dawn meal, and to place our right hands over our left hands."
"10881","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people in recitation is the one who, when he recites, recites with sorrow."
"10882","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, and Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki, (Ha), and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, they said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Tawus, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had cupping done while he was in ihram."
"10883","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Huraysh narrated to us, Salamah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had cupping done while he was fasting and in ihram."
"10884","Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to prostrate on seven bones and not to gather hair nor garment."
"10885","Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, that he heard Tawus, thinking he traced it back, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to prostrate on seven: his face, his two hands, his two knees, and his two feet, and he was forbidden to gather hair or garment."
"10886","Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi, and Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"10887","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, and Abu Khaythamah and Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki, they said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to prostrate on seven, and he was forbidden to gather his hair and his clothes."
"10888","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to prostrate on seven bones, and he forbade us to gather hair or garment."
"10889","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to prostrate on seven, and not to gather his hair or his clothes."
"10890","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd and Hammad ibn Salamah, both of them, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate on seven limbs: the nose, the forehead, the two palms, and the tips of the toes, and not to gather hair nor garment."
"10891","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim and Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to gather hair nor garment."
"10892","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to gather hair nor garment."
"10893","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and I was forbidden to gather hair or garment."
"10894","Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Mukram al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and I was forbidden to gather hair or garment."
"10895","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate on seven, and not to gather hair nor garment."
"10896","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Kamil narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to gather hair nor garment."
"10897","Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to gather hair nor garment."
"10898","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Amr ibn Yahya ibn Ufrah al-Bajali narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every condition that is not in the Book of Allah is void, even if there are a hundred conditions."
"10899","Al-Abbas al-Asfati narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it becomes edible."
"10900","Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes possession of it."
"10901","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you buy food, do not sell it until you take possession of it. Ibn Abbas said: And I consider everything else besides that among sales to be like food."
"10902","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes full possession of it; and I think everything is like it."
"10903","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hushaym narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar informed us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The food which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade to be sold until it is taken possession of."
"10904","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar informed us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling food before it is taken possession of."
"10905","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, (Ha), and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you buys food, let him not sell it until he takes possession of it."
"10906","Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Said ibn Hafs al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: We read to Maqil ibn Ubaydillah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes full possession of it."
"10907","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Musa ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling food until it is taken in full."
"10908","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah narrated to me, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Shubah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid sharecropping, but commanded that they be kind to one another."
"10909","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For one of you to grant his brother his land is better for him than to take a fixed wage."
"10910","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ibn Aishah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid renting land, but he said: For one of you to grant his brother is better for him than to take a wage for it."
"10911","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, he said: Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For a man to grant his brother his land is better for him than to take a fixed rent for it."
"10912","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding land said: Your granting it to your brother is better than your taking rent for it."
"10913","Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, (Ha), and Hamid ibn Sadan ibn Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rumh al-Misri narrated to us, both saying: al-Layth narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For one of you to grant it to his brother is better for him; and he did not forbid renting it."
"10914","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Sad ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For a man to let his brother cultivate is better for him than to take rent for it."
"10915","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, and Abdullah ibn Tawus, from Tawus, Amr said: from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Madinah enter ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfah, and the people of Syria from al-Juhfah, and the people of Yemen from Yalamlam, and the people of Najd from Qarn."
"10916","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I did zihar from my wife, and her anklet pleased me last night, so I fell upon her before expiating. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did Allah Almighty not say: Before they touch one another. Refrain until you expiate."
"10917","Sahl ibn Musa Shiran narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi informed us, Muhammad ibn Humran narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade pure silk; as for what its warp is cotton or linen, there is no harm in it."
"10918","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nashai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought out in his hand a piece of gold and a piece of silk, and said: These two are forbidden for the males of my ummah and permitted for their females."
"10919","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus and Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The first to proclaim Islam openly was Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him."
"10920","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I remain till next year, I will surely fast the ninth."
"10921","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: It is not lawful for a Muslim person who believes in Allah and the Last Day to take back his gift except the father."
"10922","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ismail, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I said: Muslim cavalry fell upon a people of polytheists and fought them, and killed their children. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are with their fathers."
"10923","Al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rabiah al-Kilabi narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Silver was never spent on anything more beloved to Allah than a sacrifice slaughtered on the day of Eid."
"10924","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, or Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing like marriage has been seen for two who love one another."
"10925","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hashim al-Basri narrated to us, Shahin ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his sermon: Only He guides to the best of morals, and only He turns away their evil."
"10926","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man gifted a she-camel to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he gave him a recompense for it, and said: Are you pleased? He said: No, so he increased him and said: Are you pleased? He said: No, so he increased him, he said: Are you pleased? He said: Yes. He said: I had intended not to accept a gift except from an Ansari or a Qurashi or a Thaqafi."
"10927","Abdan narrated to us, Ayyub al-Wazzan narrated to us, Fuhayr Yahya ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remain upon your tranquility, for emigration has ended, but there is jihad and intention, and when you are called to march forth, then march forth."
"10928","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sulayman al-Dabbas narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, do we act for what the decrees have already run with and the Pen has dried upon, or for something we begin anew? He said: Rather for what the decrees have already run with and the Pen has dried upon. He said: Then what is the point of action? He said: Act, for everyone is facilitated."
"10929","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday Surah Alif Lam Mim, the Revelation, and a surah from the Mufassal, and perhaps he said: Has there come upon man."
"10930","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Attach the fixed shares to wealth, and what the fixed shares leave, then it is for the nearest male."
"10931","Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Divide the wealth among the people of the fixed shares according to the Book of Allah, and what the fixed shares leave, then it is for the nearest male kin."
"10932","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Attach the fixed shares to the Book of Allah, and what they leave, then it is for the nearest male kin."
"10933","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Attach the fixed shares to their people, and what remains, then it is for the nearest male kin."
"10934","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The evil eye is true, and if anything were to precede the decree, the evil eye would precede it, and when you are asked to wash, then wash."
"10935","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: They used to consider umrah in the months of Hajj among the most wicked of iniquity on earth, and they used to call Muharram Safar, and say: When the back heals, and the trace is effaced, and Safar passes, then umrah becomes lawful for whoever performs umrah."
"10936","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Khayyat narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, and Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not perform umrah for Aishah in Dhu al-Hijjah except to cut off thereby the saying of the people of polytheism, for this clan of Quraysh and whoever followed their religion used to say: When the fur is restored, and the back heals, and Safar enters, then umrah becomes lawful for whoever performs umrah; so they used to forbid umrah until Dhu al-Hijjah and Muharram pass. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not perform umrah for Aishah except to nullify thereby that saying of theirs."
"10937","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had cupping done, and gave the cupper his wage, and used snuff."
"10938","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he was asked about slaughtering and shaving regarding precedence and delay, he said: No harm."
"10939","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The one who takes back his gift is like the dog that returns to its vomit."
"10940","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, (Ha). And Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, both saying: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed as miqats: for the people of Madinah Dhu al-Hulayfah, and for the people of Syria al-Juhfah, and for the people of Najd Qarn, and for the people of Yemen Yalamlam, for their people and for whoever comes upon them intending Hajj and Umrah; so whoever is short of that, then from where he begins, even the people of Makkah from Makkah."
"10941","Al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"10942","Al-Muntasir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Yunus ibn Sulayman al-Hammal narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"10943","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Sawwar ibn Muhammad ibn Quraysh al-Anbari al-Basri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding the saying of Allah Almighty: So no obscenity, nor wickedness, nor quarrelling in Hajj. He said: Obscenity is expression and exposure to women for intercourse, and wickedness is all disobedience, and quarrelling is a man quarrelling with his companion."
"10944","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to sell food until he takes full possession of it."
"10945","Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Divorce at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and two years of the caliphate of Umar, the divorce of three was one. Umar said: People have hastened a matter in which they had deliberation, so if only we enforce it upon them; so he enforced it upon them."
"10946","Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that Abu al-Sahba said to Ibn Abbas: Do you know that the three used to be made one at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr, and three years of the rule of Umar? Ibn Abbas said: Yes."
"10947","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while he was in ihram."
"10948","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to gather hair nor clothes."
"10949","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muawiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"10950","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Mutah was only forbidden because they used to trade in the middle of the year."
"10951","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, (Ha), and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, and Ibn Raja said: Muhammad ibn Talhah informed us, from Humayd ibn Wahb, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man who had dyed with henna, and said: How beautiful this is; then another passed by him who had dyed with henna and katam, and said: How beautiful this is; then another passed by him who had dyed with yellow, and said: This is better than all of this. And Tawus used to dye with yellow."
"10952","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, (Ha), and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, both saying: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting the caravans, and that a townsman sell for a Bedouin."
"10953","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The first to accept Islam was Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"10954","Al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb al-Misri narrated to us, Imran ibn Harun al-Ramli narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym al-Taifi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever splits the staff of the Muslims while the Muslims are in firm Islam, he has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck."
"10955","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Salt ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Uthman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst house is the bathhouse; voices are raised in it, and private parts are uncovered in it. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, the sick is treated in it, and dirt is removed in it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters it, let him not enter it except covered."
"10956","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Jarawi narrated to me, Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned wine, so a man said: O Messenger of Allah, we make a drink from this mizr. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"10957","Abdullah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Not permissible among sacrificial camels and cows: the one-eyed, and the emaciated; and beware of the mustalahah."
"10958","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Game meat was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he returned it, and said: We are in ihram."
"10959","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque on Friday, and there was Abu Israil standing in the sun, not seeking shade. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is wrong with him? They said: He vowed to stand and not seek shade and not break fast. He said: Command him to sit, and seek shade, and break fast."
"10960","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions arrived on the morning of the fourth, entering ihram for Hajj, so he commanded them to make it umrah. That weighed heavily upon them, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, which release? He said: The complete release."
"10961","Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Abu al-Asbagh Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Tawus, and from al-Sakhtiyani, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of a house called the bathhouse. They said: O Messenger of Allah, it removes dirt and benefits the sick. He said: Whoever enters it, let him cover himself."
"10962","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khalaf narrated to us, Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow except in what Allah is obeyed therein, and there is no vow in severing kinship, and no divorce nor emancipation in what one does not own."
"10963","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Salihi narrated to us, Umar ibn Rabbah narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a khamisah."
"10964","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, (Ha), and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, both saying: Umar ibn Rabbah narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever revives a dead land, he is most entitled to it."
"10965","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Salihi narrated to us, (Ha), and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, both saying: Umar ibn Rabbah narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands in every rakah; and al-Salihi said: at every takbir."
"10966","Sahl ibn Musa Shiran narrated to us, Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, Umar ibn Rabbah narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a woollen cloak alone."
"10967","Sahl ibn Musa narrated to us, Umar ibn Yahya narrated to us, (Ha), and Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Salihi narrated to us, both saying: Umar ibn Rabbah narrated to us, Ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cupping in the head is a cure for seven, when its practitioner intends: from madness, leprosy, vitiligo, drowsiness, toothache, headache, and darkness he finds in his eyes."
"10968","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say after the tashahhud: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the Dajjal, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and death."
"10969","Ahmad ibn Said ibn Farqad al-Juddi narrated to us, Abu Humah Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Zubaydi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Tawus, from the offspring of Tawus, informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Tawus, from his father Abdullah ibn Tawus, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): So recite what is easy of the Quran. He said: One hundred verses."
"10970","Ahmad ibn Said ibn Farqad narrated to us, Abu Humah Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Tawus, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: There is no divorce except with a waiting period, and no emancipation except for the sake of Allah Almighty."
"10971","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, (Ha), and Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Jabir, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Eid without adhan nor iqamah, then came to the women and admonished them and urged them to charity, so many a necklace and ring was thrown into the garment of Bilal until his garment was filled, or as Allah willed."
"10972","Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rafi al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Muhalhil narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: This city is sacred, Allah made it sacred, and killing was not permitted in it for anyone before me, and it was permitted for me, so it is sacred by the sanctity of Allah."
"10973","Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: There is no emigration after the conquest, but there is jihad and intention, and when you are called to march forth, then march forth."
"10974","Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rafi informed us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Muhalhil narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I travelled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Ramadan, so he fasted until he reached Usfan, then he called for a vessel and drank in it so people could see him, then he broke fast when he entered Makkah, and he conquered Makkah in Ramadan. Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted in travel and broke fast, so whoever wishes may fast and whoever wishes may break fast."
"10975","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us, Abu Muhayyah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The price of a shield at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ten dirhams."
"10976","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Hashim ibn Muhammad al-Rubayi narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah narrated to us, Said ibn Miqlas narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ayan al-Jazari, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Bathing is obligatory upon every Muslim every seven days, hair and skin, meaning on Friday. Said ibn Miqlas, he is Said ibn Abi Ayyub."
"10977","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Khushani narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of sacrifice: No deed of the son of Adam on this day is better than blood shed, except a severed kinship that is joined."
"10978","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Madini narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Isa, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not a believer of complete faith who does not count affliction as a blessing, and ease as a calamity. They said: How, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Because affliction is followed only by ease, and likewise ease is followed only by calamity; and he is not a believer of complete faith who is not in grief so long as he is not in prayer. They said: And why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Because the one praying converses with his Lord, and when he is outside prayer he converses only with the son of Adam."
"10979","Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It is from the Sunnah that your heels touch your buttocks in prayer."
"10980","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make easy and do not make difficult, and give glad tidings and do not repel, and when you become angry, be silent."
"10981","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Rabiah Fahd ibn Awf narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shared among his companions on the day of Hudaybiyah seven in a cow."
"10982","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, the brother of al-Hajjaj, narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am holding your waist-wrappers, saying: Fear the Fire, fear the prescribed punishments; then when I die I will leave you, and I am your forerunner at the Pond. Whoever comes to it has succeeded. Then some people will be brought and taken to the left, so I will say: My Lord. He will say: They kept turning back on their heels after you."
"10983","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man circumambulating the House while a man was leading him with a rein in his nose in a vow that was upon him, so he cut it and said: Lead him by his hand. And he passed by a man who had tied his hand to another person with a thong or a thread or something else besides that, so he cut it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lead him by his hand."
"10984","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Man ibn Isa narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to me, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Circumambulation of the House is prayer, but Allah Almighty permitted speech in it; so whoever speaks, let him not speak except good."
"10985","Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah Musab ibn Said narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you stands in prayer, let him not close his eyes."
"10986","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to call the Farewell Hajj the Hajj of Islam."
"10987","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only ran around the House, and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, because the polytheists saw hardship in him and his companions, so he ran."
"10988","Muhammad ibn Ahmad Abu Jafar al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, and Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The one in ihram kills the crow, the kite, the scorpion, the vicious dog, and the mouse."
"10989","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The son of Adam was commanded to prostrate on seven bones."
"10990","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Malik al-Dabbi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a shoulder blade and said: Bring me a shoulder blade, I will write for you a book after which you will never differ. Those present with him began to chatter, so a woman among those present said: Woe to you, the covenant of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to you! Some of the people said: Be silent, for you have no sense. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have no understanding."
"10991","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Ibrahim ibn Suwayd al-Nakhai narrated to us, Hilal ibn Miqlas narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me a shoulder blade and an inkpot, I will write for you a book about which no two men will differ. He said: So they delayed with the shoulder blade and the inkpot, and Allah took his soul."
"10992","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The night prayer is two by two, and the witr is one rakah at the end of the night."
"10993","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Rayyan narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Layth and Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of the Conquest the meat of dung-eating animals, their milk, and riding them."
"10994","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed tamattu until he died, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, performed tamattu until he died, and Umar and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them both, meaning the tamattu of Hajj."
"10995","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the Kabah and said: There is no god but Allah, how pure you are, and how pure your scent, and how great your sanctity; and the believer is greater in sanctity than you. Allah Almighty made you sacred, and made sacred from the believer his wealth, his blood, his honour, and that we think an evil thought of him."
"10996","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muslim ibn Sallam narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued talbiyah in umrah until he touched the Stone, and in Hajj until he stoned the Jamrah."
"10997","Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Sayrafi narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a grandmother a sixth."
"10998","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu Salih Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, (Ha), and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mualla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated to us, both saying: Sawwar ibn Musab narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The excellence of knowledge is better than worship, and the mainstay of religion is piety."
"10999","Ahmad ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, Isa ibn Sawadah al-Nakhai narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the voices of two men while they were speaking, so he asked about them, and it was said: Muawiyah and Amr ibn al-As. He said: O Allah, topple them in tribulation with toppling, and push them to the Fire with pushing."
"11000","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Ruqba is not lawful, nor umra; so whoever is given something as ruqba or umra, it is his."
"11001","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Qatan ibn Nusayr al-Dharra narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Ata and Tawus and Mujahid, from Jabir and Ibn Abbas, he said: We arrived with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intending only Hajj, so we entered ihram for Hajj, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated on his mount, touching the Corner with a staff that was with him. Then he turned to the watering place and said: Draw for me from it. They drew for him a bucket, so he took a sip, rinsed, then spat it into the bucket, then said: Return it into it. He said: O Banu Hashim, you are upon a righteous deed; were it not that you would be overcome in it or taken as a sunnah, I would have taken with you. Then he came to his dwelling and addressed his companions and said: Umrah has entered into your Hajj, so release ihram except whoever has a sacrificial animal with him. And he said: Were it not that a sacrificial animal is with me, I would have multiplied for you. Suraqah ibn Malik stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for our year or forever? He said: Rather forever. And it pleased them what coincided of his practice with the practice of the people of ignorance, and the people of ignorance used to say: When Safar passes, and the fur is restored, and the back heals, then umrah becomes lawful for whoever performs umrah."
"11002","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, al-Hayyaj ibn Bistam narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers who recognize and deny; so whoever opposes them is saved, and whoever keeps away from them is safe, and whoever mixes with them perishes."
"11003","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Sawwar ibn Musab narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid and Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity on working cows, but in every thirty a tabi, and in every forty a musinn or musinnah."
"11004","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The three used to be made one at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11005","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Harithi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Circumambulation is prayer, so lessen speech in it."
"11006","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasah al-Warraq narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever mutilates with hair, he has no share with Allah."
"11007","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Salamah, and Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that Safwan ibn Umayyah came to Madinah and slept in the mosque and placed a khamisah of his under his head, so a thief came and stole it, so he brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who ordered that his hand be cut. Safwan said: O Messenger of Allah, it is his. He said: Why not before you brought him to me."
"11008","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had cupping done, and said: Pay him."
"11009","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Many a teacher of the letters of abjad, studying stars, has no share with Allah on the Day of Resurrection."
"11010","Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Ibrahim ibn Maysarah informed me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that he mentioned the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding bathing on Friday, so I said to Ibn Abbas: And touching perfume or oil if his family has it? He said: I do not know it."
"11011","Abu Shuayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Bablutti narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to me, al-Hasan ibn Muslim narrated to me, from Tawus, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed the travel prayer as two rakahs two rakahs, and prescribed the resident prayer as four rakahs."
"11012","Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I witnessed Eid with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he began with the prayer before the sermon."
"11013","Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed while circumambulating the Kabah by a man leading a man with a nose-rein in his nose, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut it, then commanded him to lead by his hand."
"11014","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed while circumambulating the Kabah by a man who had tied his hand to another man with a thong or a thread or something else besides that, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut it and said: Lead him by your hand."
"11015","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: People used to depart in every direction, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall depart until his last contact is with the House."
"11016","Al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, Sulayman al-Ahwal informed me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood at night to pray tahajjud, said: O Allah, to You is praise, You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and who is in them, and to You is praise, You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth and who is in them, and to You is praise, You are the King of the heavens and the earth and who is in them, and to You is praise, You are the Truth and Your saying is truth, and meeting You is truth, and Paradise is truth, and Hell is truth, and the Hour is truth, and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is truth, and the prophets are truth. O Allah, to You I submitted, and in You I believed, and upon You I relied, and to You I turned, and by You I disputed, and to You I referred judgment; so forgive me what I advanced and what I delayed, and what I concealed and what I declared. You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer; there is no god but You."
"11017","Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, or another, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Hijr is from the House. Allah said: And let them circumambulate the Ancient House. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated from behind it."
"11018","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever returns in his gift is like the one who returns in his vomit."
"11019","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah on the day of sacrifice."
"11020","Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Salamah ibn Sisan al-Khayyat al-Makki narrated to us, Bishr ibn Ubayd, and he was an old shaykh, narrated to me, he said: We were with Tawus at the Maqam when we heard a commotion. He said: What is this? It was said: People whom Ibn Hisham seized in a cause and shackled. I heard Tawus narrating from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one who introduces an innovation in this ummah that did not exist, then dies until that befalls him. So I saw Ibn Hisham when he was deposed, and the workers of al-Walid came and shackled him."
"11021","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu al-Darda Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Munib narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Kaysan narrated to me, my father narrated to me, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Mujahid and Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five for five. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is five for five? He said: No people break the covenant except their enemy is given power over them, and they do not judge by other than what Allah revealed except poverty spreads among them, and indecency does not appear among them except death spreads among them, and they do not cheat the measure except they are denied vegetation and seized by years of drought, and they do not withhold zakat except rain is withheld from them."
"11022","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Junada ibn Salm narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say after the takbir and after saying: I have turned my face to the One who originated the heavens and the earth, inclining, submitting; O Allah, to You is praise, You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and whoever is in them, You are the Truth, and Your promise is true, and meeting You is true, and Paradise is true, and the Fire is true, and the Hour is true; O Allah, to You I have submitted, and in You I have believed, and upon You I have relied, and to You I turn, and by You I dispute, and to You I bring judgment, so forgive me what I sent ahead and what I delayed, and what I concealed and what I declared; O Allah, You are my God, there is no god but You. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite after this."
"11023","Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Bashir, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A leg of a wild donkey was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Kura al-Ghamir, so he returned it to its owner and apologized to him and said: We are in ihram."
"11024","Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Ata. Muhammad ibn Fudayl said: And al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his vomit."
"11025","Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud as he taught us the Quran, and he used to say: The greetings, the blessed ones, the prayers, the good things belong to Allah; peace upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Yahya ibn Bukayr said: And al-Layth used to adopt it."
"11026","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Rushdin ibn Sad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Amr ibn al-Harith, that Abu al-Zubayr narrated to him, from Ata and Tawus and Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"11027","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Tawus saying: I said to Ibn Abbas about squatting on the two feet in prayer. He said: It is the Sunna. I said: We consider it harsh for a man. He said: It is the sunna of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11028","Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his vomit."
"11029","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Muafa Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karima narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not make ruqba of your wealth; whoever gives something as ruqba, it belongs to the one to whom it was given. And ruqba is for a man to say: This is for so-and-so as long as he lives; if so-and-so dies, it is for so-and-so."
"11030","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Qutayla narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Malik, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu Mabad and Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of Muzdalifa is a standing place, and keep away from the valley of Muhassir, and all of Mina is a place of sacrifice."
"11031","Abu Hanifa Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, my uncle Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahan ibn Abi Hanifa narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Talha ibn Zayd, from Yazid ibn Sinan, from Yazid ibn Jabir al-Dimashqi, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites the sura in which the Family of Imran is mentioned on Friday, Allah and His angels send blessings upon him until the sun sets."
"11032","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Hassan al-Ziyadi narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Safwan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah, mighty and majestic, created this city on the day He created the heavens and the earth, and formed it when He formed the sun and the moon, and what is opposite it of the sky is sacred; it was not lawful for anyone before me, and it was made lawful for me only for an hour of the day, then it returned as it was. It was said to him: This Khalid ibn al-Walid is killing. He said: Rise, O so-and-so, go to Khalid ibn al-Walid and let him lift his hand from killing. The man went to him and said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: Kill whomever you can. So he killed seventy people. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached and that was mentioned to him, so he sent to Khalid and said: Did I not forbid you from killing? He said: So-and-so came to me and ordered me to kill whomever I could. He sent to him: Did I not order you? He said: You intended one thing and Allah intended another, and the command of Allah was above your command, and I could do nothing but what happened. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent about him and did not reply anything to him."
"11033","Abu al-Zinba narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani and Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no divorce except after ownership, and no manumission except after ownership."
"11034","Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: All of Arafa is a standing place, and keep away from the valley of Urana."
"11035","Abu al-Zinba narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Shaqiq ibn Bishr al-Ijli, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate upon seven limbs, and not to gather for myself a garment nor hair."
"11036","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Yazid Abu Mashar al-Barra narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn narrated to me that Tawus informed him, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We were directed upon seven bones, and we were commanded not to gather a garment nor hair."
"11037","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or grant it to his brother."
"11038","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysara, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have not seen for two who love one another anything like marriage."
"11039","Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyayna, from Ibrahim ibn Maysara, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: It is of the Sunna to touch your heels to your buttocks between the two prostrations."
"11040","Yusuf al-Qadi and Abu Khalifa narrated to us, they said: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysara, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate upon seven bones, and not to gather hair nor garment."
"11041","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, they said: Imran al-Qasir narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sad, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when he stood in the night he would say takbir, then say: O Allah, to You is praise, Sustainer of the heavens and the earth, and to You is praise, Light of the heavens and the earth, and to You is praise, Lord of the heavens and the earth and whoever is in them; You are Truth, and Your word is truth, and Your promise is truth, and meeting You is truth, and Paradise is truth, and the Fire is truth, and the Hour is truth; O Allah, to You I have submitted, and in You I have believed, and upon You I have relied, and to You I turn, and by You I dispute, and to You I bring judgment; You are our Lord and to You is the return; my Lord, forgive me what I concealed and what I declared, and what I sent ahead and what I delayed; You are my God, there is no god but You."
"11042","Ibrahim ibn Naila al-Asbahani narrated to us, Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sad, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I rubbed it off with idhkhir grass and wool, meaning semen."
"11043","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, Nuh ibn Anas al-Muqri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq informed me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We were commanded to prostrate upon seven limbs, and not to gather hair nor garment."
"11044","Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubaydillah al-Halabi narrated to me, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: It is of the Sunna in prayer to place your buttocks upon your heels between the two prostrations."
"11045","Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi narrated to us, Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq narrated to me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a woman in her litter, and she brought out a boy and said: O Prophet of Allah, does this one have a Hajj? He said: Yes, and for you is a reward."
"11046","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Samina narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymuna narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayya, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed in blind partisanship or over a thrown stone or stick, his blood money is aggravated upon his tribe; and whoever is killed by his own hand, then his retaliation is upon his own hand; and whoever stands between him and justice, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people; neither repentance nor ransom is accepted from him."
"11047","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Usayd al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn, from Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq, Ata and Tawus and Ikrima informed me, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymuna while he was in ihram."
"11048","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the eclipse prayer. He said: He recited, then bowed, then recited, then bowed, then recited, then bowed, then recited, then bowed, and the second likewise."
"11049","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiy narrated to us, Ali ibn Mabad narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, who said: I heard Tawus say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, and from a supplication that is not heard, and from a heart that is not humble, and a soul that is not satisfied; O Allah, I seek refuge in You from these four."
"11050","Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashii al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated to us, Abu Muti the judge of Balkh narrated to us, from al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Umara, from al-Hakam, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while in Mina: If the people of the gathering knew with whom they have alighted they would rejoice at the bounty from their Lord after forgiveness."
"11051","Ahmad ibn Ziyad ibn Zakariyya al-Iyadi narrated to us at Jabala, Yazid ibn Qays narrated to us, Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from al-Hakam ibn Utayba, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while in Mina saying: If the people of the gathering knew with whom they have alighted they would rejoice at the bounty after forgiveness."
"11052","Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salim narrated to me, from al-Zubaydi, Isa ibn Yazid narrated to us that Tawus Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated to them: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha prayer one night until the people of the mosque turned away except Uthman ibn Mazun, who was of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and fifteen men or sixteen, not reaching seventeen. Uthman said: I will not leave tonight until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) comes out and I pray with him and know his affair. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out close to a third of the night, and with him was Bilal, and he saw no one in the mosque when he heard a murmur of their speech in a corner of the mosque. He walked to them until he greeted them and said: What keeps you seated at this hour? They said: We waited for you to witness the prayer with you. He said to them: No nation before you ever prayed this prayer of yours, and you have remained in prayer since. And he said: The stars are the security of the sky; when the stars are effaced, there comes to the sky what it is promised; and I am the security of my companions, so when I am gone, there comes to my companions what they are promised; and my companions are the security of my nation, so when my companions are gone, there comes to my nation what it is promised."
"11053","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no one I praise except the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11054","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya al-Muallim narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever his prayer does not forbid him from indecency and evil only increases in distance from Allah."
"11055","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yala ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi narrated to us, from his father, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from Layth, from Ata and Tawus and Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar and Jabir, may Allah be pleased with them: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions did not circumambulate between Safa and Marwa except one circumambulation for their Hajj and their Umra."
"11056","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The son of Adam has three hundred and sixty joints; upon each one of them is a charity every day. He said: A good word a man speaks is a charity, and a man helping his brother with something is a charity, and a drink of water he gives him is a charity, and removing harm from the road is a charity."
"11057","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki and Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Bazzar al-Asbahani narrated to us, they said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Ghawth ibn Ghaylan ibn Munabbih al-Sanani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Safwan narrated to us, from Idris son of the daughter of Wahb ibn Munabbih, Wahb ibn Munabbih narrated to me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for what has touched the Corner of the impurities of ignorance and its filth, and the hands of oppressors and sinners, healing would be sought by it from every ailment, and it would be cast today as it was on the day Allah created it; Allah only changed it to black lest the people of the world look upon the adornment of Paradise, and that they may be patient toward it. It is a ruby of the rubies of Paradise which Allah placed when Adam was sent down at the site of the Kaba before the Kaba existed, while the earth that day was pure and no disobedience had been done in it, and it had no people to defile it. A rank of angels was placed for it at the boundaries of the sanctuary guarding it from the inhabitants of the earth, whose inhabitants that day were the jinn; it was not fitting for them to look at it, for it is something of Paradise. The angels drove them away from it while they stood at the boundaries of the sanctuary gazing at it from every side, and for that it was called the sanctuary, for they come between them and it."
"11058","Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mundhir ibn al-Numan informed us, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Twelve thousand will come out from Aden Abyan aiding Allah and His Messenger; they are the best of those between me and them."
"11059","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Musa al-Yamani, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from Ibn Abbas, in a raised report, who said: Whoever heads to the desert becomes harsh, and whoever follows game becomes heedless, and whoever comes to the ruler is tempted."
"11060","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hassan al-Kufi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Musa, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None who commits intercourse with a close unmarriageable relative enters Paradise."
"11061","Al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Idris son of the daughter of Wahb ibn Munabbih, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It suffices you as sin that you remain constantly disputing."
"11062","Al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, Abd narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Idris ibn Munabbih, from his father Wahb ibn Munabbih, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Jibril, peace be upon him, to see him in his form. He said: Call upon your Lord. So he called upon his Lord, and a darkness rose upon him from the east and kept rising and spreading; when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him he fell unconscious, so he came to him and revived him and wiped the spittle from his cheek."
"11063","Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ulatha narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The death of a stranger is martyrdom when he is dying: he casts his sight to his right and to his left and sees none but a stranger, and he remembers his family and his child, and breathes; for every breath he breathes Allah effaces two million evil deeds and writes for him two million good deeds."
"11064","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Mujahid, who said: Ibn Abbas said about the prostration of Sad: The repentance of a prophet whom Allah commanded His Prophet to follow."
"11065","Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Murra narrated to us, Shuba informed us. And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Marzuq, who said: I heard Mujahid saying: Ibn Abbas was asked about prostration in Sad, and he said: Those are they whom Allah guided, so follow their guidance."
"11066","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Hisham narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amr ibn Murra, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey while he was reciting Sura Sad, and he prostrated in it."
"11067","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas about His word: And We gave you seven of the oft-repeated. He said: They are the seven long suras."
"11068","Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped on the back of his foot while fasting."
"11069","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Kissing was permitted for the old man while fasting, and the young man was forbidden it."
"11070","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi narrated to us. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal and Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us. And Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, Mualla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, they said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Allah, mighty and majestic, obligated prayer upon the tongue of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): in residence four, and on journey two, and in fear one."
"11071","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Abu Mamar al-Qatii narrated to us, they said: al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Aidh, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The prayer of residence is four, and of journey two, and of fear one."
"11072","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Jafar al-Ramli narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Harith al-Ghanawi, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Allah obligated prayer upon the tongue of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): in residence four, and on journey two, and in fear one."
"11073","Yusuf al-Qadi and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shuba informed us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was aided by the east wind, and Ad were destroyed by the west wind."
"11074","Yusuf and Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, they said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shuba informed us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: This is an Umra we enjoyed; whoever has no sacrificial animal with him, let him exit into full release, for Umra has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."
"11075","Ibrahim ibn Naila al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Abu Maryam narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only made it an Umra, for they came to Mecca four nights before Arafa, and he disliked that the Muslims remain four nights without circumambulating the House, and he knew that when they circumambulated the House they would exit ihram except one who had driven a sacrificial animal, so he said: An Umra we enjoyed, three times, then Umra entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."
"11076","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hammad ibn Numayr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I was given five that no prophet before me was given: I was sent to the red and the black, while a prophet would be sent only to his own people; and I was aided by awe, so that the enemy fear me from a march of a month or two months; and spoils were made lawful for me and were not lawful for those before me; and the earth was made for me a mosque and a purification; and it was said to me: Ask and you shall be given, so I stored my supplication as intercession for my nation, and it will reach, Allah willing, whoever dies not associating anything with Allah."
"11077","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam and Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said a day before Tarwiya: Our lodging tomorrow, Allah willing, is at the right side of al-Khayf where the polytheists divided by oaths."
"11078","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ansari narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: al-Fadl was older than me, and he would mount me behind him so I was in front of him; I mounted with my brother behind a donkey, and we reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying with the people at Arafa, so we dismounted before him and entered and prayed, and we left it grazing before him, and he did not break his prayer."
"11079","Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Hasan ibn Umara, from al-Hakam ibn Utayba, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: It is of the Sunna that a man not pray with one tayammum except one prayer, then he performs tayammum for the next prayer."
"11080","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ayyub ibn Rashid al-Basri narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi and al-Hakam ibn Utayba narrated to me, from Miqsam and Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over Hamza and looked at what had been done to him, he said: Were it not that women would grieve I would not have buried him, and I would have left him until he is in the bellies of beasts and the crops of birds until Allah raises him from there. He said: And what he saw of him grieved him, so he said: If I prevail over Quraysh I shall mutilate thirty men of them. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed about that: If you punish, then punish with the like of what you were afflicted with, to His word: they plot. Then he ordered him prepared toward the qibla, then magnified over him nine takbirs, then gathered the martyrs over him; whenever a martyr was brought he was placed beside Hamza, and he prayed over him and over the martyrs with him, until he prayed over him and over the martyrs seventy-two prayers. Then he stood over his companions until he buried them. When the Quran came down the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pardoned and overlooked and left mutilation."
"11081","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Jabara ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, Abu Shayba Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Raid and you will gain the daughters of the yellow ones. Some hypocrites said: He tempts you with women. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: And of them is he who says: Grant me leave and do not tempt me."
"11082","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shabib al-Asbahani al-Assal narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Hakam narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled in Ramadan and fasted and broke fast; whoever wishes fasts, and whoever wishes breaks fast."
"11083","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Two verses of Sura al-Maida were abrogated: the verse of the sacrificial animals and the garlands, and the other verse: So judge between them or turn away from them. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given choice in that: if he wished he judged between them, and if he wished he referred them to the judgment of another, until there came down: So judge between them by what Allah revealed."
"11084","Umar ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from his father, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, who said: It is disliked to drink from the ear of the cup and the crack of the cup."
"11085","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Fadl ibn Muwaffaq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was aided by awe at a march of two months against his enemy."
"11086","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughira, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Isa and Musa and Ibrahim, peace be upon them: as for Isa, he is red, curly, broad-chested; and as for Musa, he is dark, corpulent, lank-haired, as if of the men of al-Zutt. They said to him: And Ibrahim? He said: Look at your companion."
"11087","Al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Muawiya narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: All flies are in the Fire except the bee."
"11088","Abu al-Zinba narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abu Muslim narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, I think from Ibn Abbas, who said: If a man of the people of al-Awali would invite the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at midnight over barley bread, he would accept."
"11089","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad Arara narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shuba, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House upon his riding animal, touching the Corner with his staff."
"11090","Al-Mamari and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Salam ibn Salih al-Harawi narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the city of knowledge, and Ali is its gate; whoever wants knowledge, let him come to it through its gate."
"11091","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Rawh ibn Musafir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out when he went out to Banu Qurayza upon a donkey, and with him was Jibril, peace be upon him, upon a white mule with a velvet blanket of brocade under him, its pile bearing the banner. He marched a while, then Jibril, peace be upon him, said: O Muhammad, by the One who sent you with the truth, I shall not descend from it until it is opened for you. Ibn Abbas said: And he did not return until it was opened for him."
"11092","Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Milhan ibn Sulayman al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dawud al-Khuraybi narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Ali and Fatima while they were laughing; when they saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they fell silent. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: What is with you? You were laughing, and when you saw me you fell silent? Fatima hastened and said: May my father be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, he said: I am dearer to the Messenger of Allah than you, so I said: Rather I am dearer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: O my little daughter, you have the tenderness of a child, and Ali is dearer to me than you."
"11093","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Sabuni al-Tustari narrated to us, Abbad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Musa ibn Umayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, about: Peace upon the family of Yasin. He said: We are the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11094","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to us, Salama ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: When the verse came down: In it are men who love to purify themselves, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Uwaymir ibn Saida and said: What is this purification for which Allah, mighty and majestic, praised you? They said: O Messenger of Allah, no man or woman of us comes from relieving himself except he washes his private part, or he said: his seat. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is this."
"11095","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while in Mecca toward Bayt al-Maqdis with the Kaba before him, and after he emigrated for sixteen months, then he turned toward the Kaba."
"11096","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of domestic donkeys, and pregnant women to be approached until they deliver what is in their wombs, and eating every fanged beast of prey, and selling spoils until divided, and killing children."
"11097","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shuba informed us. And Muhammad ibn Asad ibn Yazid al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: Fear Allah as He should be feared, the verse, and said: If a drop of Zaqqum dripped into the seas of the world it would spoil their livelihoods; how then with one whose food it is?"
"11098","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that he held the exception permissible even after a year, then recited: And do not say of anything: I shall do that tomorrow, except if Allah wills, and remember your Lord when you forget. He says: When you remember. It was said to al-Amash: Did you hear this from Mujahid? He said: al-Layth narrated it to me from Mujahid."
"11099","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Jafar al-Madini narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Humayd al-Araj, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: That some youths of Banu Hashim came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, employ us over this charity; we shall take from it what people take, and render as they render. He said: We, the family of Muhammad, charity is not lawful for us, and it is the filth of people; but what do you think: when I take hold of the ring of Paradise, would I prefer anyone over you?"
"11100","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Musab ibn Abdillah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid and Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Tawus and Ata, they informed him, from Ibn Abbas, that he informed them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to combine Zuhr and Asr, and combine Maghrib and Isha on journey without being hastened by any affair, nor pursued by an enemy, nor fearing anything."
"11101","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I was in the house of my aunt Maymuna; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose in the night and performed ablution, so I stood on his left, and he turned me with his hands and placed me on his right."
"11102","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined on journey and in residence Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha."
"11103","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Salih ibn Abdillah al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam began strange, and it shall return strange; so glad tidings to the strangers."
"11104","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Salih al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Hour there are trials like pieces of the dark night: a man wakes in them a believer and evenings a disbeliever, and evenings a believer and wakes a disbeliever; in them a people sell their religion for a portion of the world."
"11105","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be cupped on the fifteenth, or the seventeenth, or the nineteenth, or the twenty-first, lest the blood rage with you and kill you."
"11106","Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Abu Khaythama Musab ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has three born to him and does not name one of them Muhammad has shown ignorance."
"11107","Ahmad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Khaythama Musab ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of kindness in this world are the people of kindness in the Hereafter."
"11108","Muhammad ibn al-Farah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved deeds to Allah after the obligations is bringing joy to the Muslim."
"11109","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of the conquest of Mecca carrion-eating animals, and plunder."
"11110","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami al-Misri narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Habib narrated to us, Sallam al-Tawil narrated to us, from Hamza al-Zayyat, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts the day of Arafa, it is an expiation for two years."
"11111","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Habib narrated to us, Sallam al-Tawil narrated to us, from Hamza al-Zayyat, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts a day of Muharram, for every day are thirty good deeds."
"11112","Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, Mindal narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not honor the elder, and have mercy on the young, and command good, and forbid evil."
"11113","Al-Hasan ibn Alawiyyah al-Qattan narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sukkari narrated to us, Musa ibn Abi Sulaym al-Basri narrated to us, Mindal narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, among the garden palms of Medina; we passed a garden, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: How beautiful this garden is, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Your garden in Paradise is more beautiful than it. Then he pointed with his hand to his head and his beard, then wept until his weeping rose. It was said: What makes you weep? He said: Rancors in the chests of a people who will not reveal them to you until they lose me."
"11114","Salama ibn Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Yahya ibn Salama ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given five no prophet before me was given: I was sent to all people, the red and the black, while a prophet would be sent only to his people; and I was aided by awe, my enemy fears me at a march of a month; and spoils were given to me; and the earth was made for me a mosque and a purification; and I was given intercession, and I deferred it for my nation on the Day of Resurrection."
"11115","Salama narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said on the night I was taken by night: I saw Ibrahim, and he resembles me; and I saw Musa, tall, curly, as if of the men of Shanu'a; and I saw Isa, red, of medium stature, lank-haired, as if his head drips oil."
"11116","Salama narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa."
"11117","Salama narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the Farewell Hajj: I shall surely kill the Amalekites in a battalion. Jibril, peace be upon him, said: Or Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him."
"11118","Salama ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that he used to recite this reading: Arrogant therein, conversing by night, shunning. He said: The polytheists used to shun the Messenger in their poetry."
"11119","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Harithi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salama ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Speech is disliked in four places: Friday, the day of Fitr, the day of Adha, and in seeking rain when the imam ascends the pulpit, so he speaks until he descends."
"11120","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hashim al-Balabakki narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Dinar narrated to me, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, how is ablution? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water for ablution and washed his right hand three times, then put his hand into the vessel, then rinsed his mouth and nose three times each, then wiped his head and the outside of his ears along with his head, then washed his feet three times. Then he said: Such is ablution; whoever adds to this has transgressed and wronged."
"11121","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Hamid ibn Adam al-Marwazi narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between his companions, between the Emigrants and the Helpers, and did not make brotherhood between Ali ibn Abi Talib and any of them, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, went out angry until he came to a rivulet of land and pillowed his arm, and the wind blew dust upon him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought him until he found him and nudged him with his foot and said to him: Rise; you are fit to be none but Abu Turab. Are you angry with me because I made brotherhood between the Emigrants and the Helpers and did not make brotherhood between you and any of them? Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except there is no prophet after me? Whoever loves you is encompassed by security and faith, and whoever hates you, Allah shall make him die the death of ignorance, and he shall be reckoned for his deed in Islam."
"11122","Sa'id ibn Abd Rabbih al-Saffar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ali ibn Jamil al-Raqqi narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise is a tree, or: there is no tree in Paradise - Ali ibn Jamil doubted - upon which there is no leaf except written upon it: There is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, Umar al-Faruq, Uthman Dhu al-Nurayn."
"11123","Al-Muntasir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntasir al-Baghdadi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Hammad Sajjada narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, I think he raised it, who said: When the sun sets, restrain your children, for it is an hour in which devils spread."
"11124","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ayyub al-Razi narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, I think he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Two greedy ones never satisfy their greed: one greedy in seeking knowledge, and one greedy in seeking the world."
"11125","Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in Sad."
"11126","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiy narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Aban ibn Salih, from Mujahid, who said: I presented the codex to Ibn Abbas from its opening to its seal, stopping him at every verse of it and asking him about it, until I reached this verse: Your women are a tillage for you, so come to your tillage as you wish. Ibn Abbas said: This clan of Quraysh in Mecca used to explain women and enjoy them facing and from behind; when they came to Medina and married among the Ansar and went to do with them so, they disapproved of that and said: This is something never done; the report spread until it reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed about that: Your women are a tillage for you, so come to your tillage as you wish: facing, and if you wish kneeling; he only means thereby the place of offspring for tillage. He says: Come to the tillage from where you wish. Ibn Abbas said: Ibn Umar said: In her rear; so Ibn Umar erred, and Allah forgive him; the report was only upon this."
"11127","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman nephew of Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Abu Tumayla Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, from Abu Hamza, from Jabir, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever calls the adhan seven years seeking reward, a clearance from the Fire is written for him."
"11128","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Rawh ibn Janah narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One jurist is harder upon Satan than a thousand worshippers."
"11129","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Hurayth narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, Raja ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of them are those easiest in dowry."
"11130","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abu al-Harith, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh said: and he is Raja, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The best of them are those easiest in dowry."
"11131","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abdillah al-Mawsili narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shares in unlawful blood by half a word comes on the Day of Resurrection with written between his eyes: Despairing of the mercy of Allah."
"11132","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting and in ihram."
"11133","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine, so keep clean of it."
"11134","And with his chain, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Muslims are partners in three: fire, water, and pasture, and its price is unlawful."
"11135","Abdan narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man with a wound seeking his permission to lance it, and he permitted him."
"11136","Abdan narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Treat well my uncle al-Abbas, for he is the remainder of my fathers; a man's paternal uncle is the like of his father."
"11137","Abdan narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for me and said: What an excellent interpreter you are; and Jibril supplicated for me twice."
"11138","Abdan narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When Umar embraced Islam, Jibril, peace be upon him, descended and said: O Muhammad, the people of heaven have rejoiced at the Islam of Umar."
"11139","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, I think he raised it, who said: Seek good and needs from those of handsome faces."
"11140","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came announcing the funeral to people, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, ask Allah for your dead, and do not announce them to people."
"11141","Abdan narrated to us, Zayd narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from al-Awwam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar used to bring the dead into the grave from the side of the qibla."
"11142","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beautify your voices with the Quran."
"11143","Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abda ibn Abi Lubaba, from Miqsam and Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, about: Allah is the Guardian of those who believe; He brings them out of darkness into light. He said: They are a people who had disbelieved in Isa and believed in Muhammad; and: And those who disbelieve, their guardians are taghut; they bring them out of light into darkness. They are a people who believed in Isa, and when Muhammad was sent they disbelieved in him."
"11144","Al-Hadrami narrated to us, Layth ibn Harun al-Ukli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon the pulpit he said Amin three times, and he was asked about that, so he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: Whoever you are mentioned before and he does not send blessings upon you, Allah cast him away; say Amin, so I said Amin. He said: Whoever reaches his parents or one of them and dies unforgiven, Allah cast him away; say Amin, so I said Amin. And whoever reaches Ramadan and is not forgiven, Allah cast him away; say Amin, so I said Amin."
"11145","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no days greater before Allah, nor deeds therein dearer to Him, than the ten days; so increase therein glorification, magnification, and declaration of oneness."
"11146","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as pilgrims, and he ordered them and they made it an Umra, then said: Had I faced of my affair what I now look back upon, I would have done as they did; but Umra has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection. Then he interlaced his fingers together. The people exited ihram except one who had the sacrificial animal with him. Ali came from Yemen, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: With what did you enter ihram? He said: I entered ihram with what you entered ihram with. He said: Do you have a sacrificial animal with you? He said: No. He said: Then remain as you are, and for you is a third of my sacrificial animal. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had gifted a hundred camels."
"11147","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, they said: Hushaym narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad informed us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Hajj; when he came he circumambulated the House and between Safa and Marwa, and did not shorten nor exit ihram, he who had driven the sacrificial animal; and he ordered one who had not driven the sacrificial animal to circumambulate, and to run, and to shorten or shave, then exit ihram."
"11148","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: I heard Israil mentioning from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a man whose thigh was exposed and said: Cover it, for a man's thigh is of his nakedness."
"11149","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Missisi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine, so keep clean from urine."
"11150","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you is unable against the enemy to strive against him, and against the night to endure it, let him increase remembrance of Allah."
"11151","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting to say: I am with Allah better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"11152","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Qutba ibn Abd al-Aziz, from al-Amash, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade inciting beasts against one another."
"11153","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja informed us, Israil informed us, from Muslim al-Awar, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was born on Monday, and revelation came upon him on Monday, and he died on Monday."
"11154","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja informed us, Israil informed us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not to burden my nation, I would have imposed the toothstick upon them at every prayer."
"11155","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja informed us, Israil informed us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe from behind chambers, and no one ever saw his nakedness."
"11156","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The ring of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a circle of silver."
"11157","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed his sacrificial animal on the day he was blocked, at al-Tanim."
"11158","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon a mat."
"11159","Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, about His word: O Prophet, why do you forbid what Allah made lawful for you. He said: He forbade his concubine to himself."
"11160","Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled in Ramadan and fasted a day until Asr, then broke fast, then fasted and completed the fast until night."
"11161","Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated and ran the first three to show the polytheists that he and his companions had strength, and walked the four."
"11162","Al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that my nation would be weakened, I would have commanded them with the toothstick at every prayer."
"11163","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, about His word: And those of your women who commit indecency, to His word: until death takes them. He said: They were confined in houses: if she died she died, and if she lived she lived, until this verse in al-Nur came down: The fornicatress and the fornicator, flog each one of them a hundred lashes, and the sura of prescribed punishments came down; whoever did anything was flogged and released."
"11164","Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Muslim al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the dead is buried he hears the striking of their sandals when they turn away from him departing."
"11165","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail al-Nahdi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear a shirt short in sleeves and length."
"11166","11137 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati and al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat narrated to us, they said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us (h), and Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shabib al-Assal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, they both said: al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: ""He performed Umrah in Ramadan."""
"11167","11138 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Said ibn Hafs al-Nufayli narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Fitr ibn Khalifah, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""The beginning of this affair is prophethood and mercy, then there will be caliphate and mercy, then there will be kingship and mercy, then there will be emirate and mercy, then they will jostle over it like donkeys jostle, so upon you is jihad, and indeed the best of your jihad is ribat, and indeed the best of your ribat is Asqalan."""
"11168","11139 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Abu al-Ashhab al-Kufi, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Abdullah ibn Kathir, from Mujahid, he said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas when a man came to him and said: O Abu Abbas, I divorced my wife three times. Ibn Abbas said: ""You have disobeyed your Lord, and your wife is separated from you. Allah Almighty said: (O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them facing their waiting period)."""
"11169","11140 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ubaydah al-Tammar narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Saj, from Khusayf, from Mujahid and Ikrimah and Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Wiping over the two khuffs was mentioned in the presence of Umar and Sad and Abdullah ibn Umar, so Umar and Sad said: He has understood. Ibn Abbas said: O Sad, do you not remember that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiped, but did he wipe after Surah al-Maidah was revealed?"
"11170","11141 - al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us, Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""The pen is lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the insane until he recovers, and from the child until he reasons or reaches puberty."""
"11171","11142 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Harun ibn Harun, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""The ruin of my ummah is in three: in partisanship, and the Qadariyyah, and narrating without verification."""
"11172","11143 - al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, regarding the saying of Allah Almighty {And remember your Lord when you forget}, he said: ""When you forget the exception, then make the exception when you remember, and it is specific to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we are not to make the exception except within the continuity of the oath."""
"11173","11144 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Qazah ibn Suwayd al-Bahili narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: ""I do not ask you for any reward for what I have brought you of proofs and guidance except that you love Allah and draw near to Him through obedience to Him."""
"11174","11145 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, they said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade on the day of Khaybar selling the spoils of war before they are divided."
"11175","11146 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Musab ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade on the day of Khaybar intercourse with pregnant women and said: ""You water your water to another's crop,"" and forbade selling the spoils before they are divided, and eating the meat of domestic donkeys, and every fanged beast of prey."
"11176","11147 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, the author of al-Maghazi, narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Najih said: Mujahid narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gifted in the year of al-Hudaybiyyah a camel among his sacrificial animals to Abu Jahl, with a silver nose-ring on its head, to enrage thereby the polytheists."
"11177","11148 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gifted in the Umrah of al-Hudaybiyyah the camel of Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, with a gold bridle upon it, and it is the halter, and he did that only to enrage Quraysh."
"11178","11149 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-Asqalani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman Abu Sulayman al-Madini narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to go out in battle in the path of Allah. He said: ""Upon you is al-Sham, for Allah Almighty has guaranteed al-Sham and its people for me, and stay in Asqalan of al-Sham, for when the millstone turns among my ummah its people will be in good and well-being."""
"11179","11150 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us (h), and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""O Allah, forgive those who shave."" They said: And those who shorten. He said on the third: ""And those who shorten."""
"11180","11151 - Abu Hanifah Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Wasiti and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Whoever flees from two has fled, and whoever flees from three has not fled."""
"11181","11152 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, Husayn al-Ashqar narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: ""The forerunners are three: the forerunner to Musa is Yusha ibn Nun, and the forerunner to Isa is the companion of Yasin, and the forerunner to Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is Ali ibn Abi Talib."""
"11182","11153 - Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married Ali, Fatimah said: O Messenger of Allah, you have married me to a poor man who has nothing. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Are you not pleased, O Fatimah, that Allah Almighty chose from the people of the earth two men, one of them your father and the other your husband."""
"11183","11154 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Salih al-Harawi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married Ali to Fatimah, she said: You have married me to a destitute man with no wealth. He said to her: ""Are you not pleased that Allah looked upon the earth and chose from it two men, making one of them your father and the other your husband."""
"11184","11155 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Abban ibn Taghlib, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, {Then pursuit in a fitting way and payment to him with excellence}, he said: ""The Children of Israel, when one of them was killed deliberately, nothing was lawful for them except retaliation, and blood-money was made lawful for you. So this one is commanded to pursue fittingly, and this one is commanded to pay with excellence, {That is alleviation from your Lord}."""
"11185","11156 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to us, Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Anbasah narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Khalid, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded Ali to distribute his sacrificial animals, so he distributed them in portions, then he came to him and he said: ""Distribute their coverings and their skins."""
"11186","11157 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih and Humayd al-Araj, that a man asked Ibn Abbas and said: He divorced his wife a hundred times. He said: ""You have disobeyed your Lord, and your wife is separated from you, for you did not fear Allah so that He would make for you a way out and provide for you from whence you do not expect."" And he recited: {O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them for their waiting period}."
"11187","11158 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Abbas Sahib al-Shamah narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, some of our companions narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""When you pass by the gardens of Paradise, graze."" It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the gardens of Paradise? He said: ""The gatherings of knowledge."""
"11188","11159 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not fight a people until he called them."
"11189","11160 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to us, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sayf ibn Sulayman, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Jews used to say: This world is seven thousand years, and we shall only be punished for each thousand years a day in the Fire, and they are but numbered days. So Allah Almighty revealed concerning that: {And they said: The Fire will not touch us except for numbered days}, up to His saying: {Abiding therein}."
"11190","11161 - al-Mamari narrated to us, Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Said ibn Awad al-Makki narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade sleeping before the Isha prayer, and talking after it."
"11191","11162 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Ibn Mujahid narrated to us, from his father and Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""O people of Makkah, do not shorten the prayer at less than four barids from Makkah to Usfan."""
"11192","11163 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham al-Muadhhdhin narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Mujahid narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: This verse was revealed concerning the Qadariyyah: {On the Day they are dragged into the Fire on their faces: Taste the touch of Saqar. Indeed, all things We created with measure}."
"11193","11164 - Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Mujahid narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, regarding the saying of Allah Almighty: {Those who spend their wealth by night and day, secretly and openly}, he said: ""It was revealed concerning Ali ibn Abi Talib; he had four dirhams, so he spent one by night, one by day, one in secret, and one openly."""
"11194","11165 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qays ibn Sad narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Zamzam, so we drew for him a bucket, and he drank, then spat into the bucket, then we poured it into Zamzam, then he said: ""Were it not that you would be overcome over it, I would draw with my own hand."""
"11195","11166 - Abu Hanifah Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr al-Salimi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Rabah ibn Abi Maruf al-Makki, from Qays ibn Sad, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""A man will enter Paradise, and no household or chamber in Paradise will remain but they will say: Welcome, welcome to us."" Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the reward of this man on that day? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Yes, and you are he, O Abu Bakr."""
"11196","11167 - Musa ibn Harun and Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, they said: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Hurrah, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""The best water on the face of the earth is the water of Zamzam, in it is food from nourishment and healing from sickness, and the worst water on the face of the earth is water in the valley of Barahut in Hadramawt, like the legs of locusts of vermin; in the morning it flows and in the evening there is no moisture in it."""
"11197","11168 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruasi narrated to us, Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""None shall enter Paradise who is addicted to wine, nor disobedient to parents, nor one who reminds of favors."""
"11198","11169 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muawiyah al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""There will come in the last times peoples whose faces are the faces of humans and whose hearts are the hearts of devils, like ravenous wolves; there is nothing of mercy in their hearts, shedders of blood, not refraining from evil. If you follow them they deceive you, if you hide from them they backbite you, if they speak to you they lie to you, if you trust them they betray you. Their child is insolent, their youth is wicked, their elder neither commands good nor forbids evil. Pride through them is humiliation, seeking what is in their hands is poverty. The forbearing among them is misguided, the commander of good among them is accused, the believer among them is oppressed, the sinner among them is honored. The Sunnah among them is innovation, and innovation among them is Sunnah. At that time the worst of them will be given power over them, and their best will supplicate and will not be answered."""
"11199","11170 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Abbad narrated to us, Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""None shall enter Paradise who is addicted to wine, nor disobedient to parents, nor one who reminds of favors."" Ibn Abbas said: That weighed upon me, for believers commit sins, until I found that in the Book of Allah concerning the disobedient: {So would you perhaps, if you turned away, cause corruption on earth and sever your ties of kinship}, the verse, and concerning the one who reminds: {Do not invalidate your charities with reminders and injury}, the verse, and concerning wine: {Wine and gambling and idols and divining arrows are but defilement}, up to His saying: {So avoid it}."
"11200","11171 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ubaydullah al-Ghudani narrated to us, al-Mualla ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Indeed the angels rejoice at the passing of winter, out of mercy for what befalls the poor believers of hardship."""
"11201","11172 - Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abd al-Karim informed me, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I and al-Fadl ran ahead of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, riding a donkey while he was praying on the day of Arafah, with no one between us and him to come between us and him."
"11202","11173 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abu Bishr, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, regarding the saying of Allah Almighty: {You will surely ride stage upon stage}, he said: ""Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."""
"11203","11174 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yazid al-Narsi al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abu Umar Hafs ibn Umar al-Muqaddami al-Zawzani narrated to us, Abu Muhammad al-Yazidi narrated to us, Abu Amr ibn al-Ala narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that he used to read: ({And it is not for a prophet to embezzle}), and how could it not be for him to embezzle while he may be killed. Allah said: {And they kill the prophets}. But the hypocrites accused the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning something, so Allah Almighty revealed: ({And it is not for a prophet to embezzle})."
"11204","11175 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Nasai al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Ibrahim al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu al-Ala ibn Amr narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Whatever is in the Quran as qattal with shaddah is punishment, and whatever is qatal with lightness is mercy."
"11205","11176 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abu Mashar al-Barra Yusuf ibn Yazid narrated to us, Mayyah ibn Sari narrated to us, from Mujahid, that a Kufan man asked Ibn Abbas about nabidh of the jar, so Ibn Abbas put his two fingers in his ears and said: May they be deaf if I lie against the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; I heard him say: ""All mud is unlawful, its white and its red and its black and its green."""
"11206","11177 - al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Duri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sulaym, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Ashqar narrated to me, Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Abu Hashim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""The two feet of a servant shall not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about four: about his life in what he spent it, about his body in what he wore it out, about his wealth in what he spent it and from where he earned it, and about our love, the people of the house."""
"11207","11178 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Sallam al-Tawil narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrating upon his garment."
"11208","Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit from Ibn Abbas. 11179 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Qurmuti narrated to us, Harun ibn Musa al-Harawi narrated to us, Abu Damrah narrated to us, from Ibn Saman, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: ""Perhaps you will remain after me until you meet a people who deny the decree of Allah, attributing sins against His servants; they derived their speech from Christianity. When that happens, disavow yourselves to Allah from them."" Ibn Abbas would raise his hands and say: ""O Allah, I disavow myself to You from them as Your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded."""
"11209","Ubayd ibn Umayr from Ibn Abbas. 11180 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: ""The son of Adam is commanded to prostrate upon seven bones."""
"11210","11181 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Ayli narrated to me, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Iblis said to his Lord: O Lord, Adam has been sent down, and I know there will be a book and messengers, so what are their book and their messengers? He said: He said: Their messengers are the angels and the prophets among them, and their books are the Torah, the Psalms, the Gospel, and the Furqan. He said: So what is my book? He said: Your book is tattooing, your recitation is poetry, your messengers are soothsayers, your food is that over which the name of Allah is not mentioned, your drink is every intoxicant, your truth is lying, your house is the bathhouse, your snares are women, your caller is the flute, and your mosque is the markets."""
"11211","Amr ibn Dinar from Ibn Abbas. 11182 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Abi Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Dating began in the year in which the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Madinah, and in it Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr was born."
"11212","11183 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Malik ibn Ziyad al-Kufi narrated to us, Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Whoever is given a gift while people are with him, they are partners with him in it."""
"11213","11184 - Abdullah ibn Musa ibn Abi Uthman al-Anmati narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Ulayy narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata and Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: ""Whoever looks at a gap in a row, let him fill it himself; if he does not do so and a passer passes, let him step over his neck, for he has no sanctity."""
"11214","11185 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged by the oath and the single witness."
"11215","11186 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub Sahib al-Maghazi narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The wives of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to dye with henna while in ihram, and wear saffron-dyed garments while in ihram."
"11216","11187 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Shibl ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Dinar narrating from Jabir and Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling fruit until its soundness appears."
"11217","11188 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Said ibn Hafs al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: We read to Maqil ibn Ubaydullah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Do not sell fruit until its soundness appears."""
"11218","11189 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he attended a funeral, gloom was seen upon him, and he spoke much to himself."
"11219","11190 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was at al-Uthayah when he was brought henna blossom, and he said: ""It resembles the basil of Paradise."""
"11220","11191 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar and Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he passed by this verse: {By the soul and what proportioned it, then inspired it its wickedness and its piety}, would stop, then say: ""O Allah, grant my soul its piety; You are its guardian and master and the best to purify it."""
"11221","11192 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that Ibn Abbas said: Whoever meets Allah associating nothing with Him and not killing a soul, meets Allah with a light back."
"11222","11193 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: ""Do not persist in looking at lepers."""
"11223","11194 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Kalai narrated to us, Zayn ibn Shuayb al-Iskandarani narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, consummated marriage with his maternal aunt Maymunah at Sarif, and she died at Sarif. al-Layth ibn Sad said: ""Zayn ibn Shuayb was as named, Zayn."""
"11224","11195 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Khawwas al-Mawsili narrated to us, Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Umar ibn Habib al-Makki, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that a man freed a slave of his, then the emancipator died, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave the inheritance of the freed one."
"11225","11196 - Ahmad ibn Shuayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Sayf Abu Dawud al-Harrani narrated to us, Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated to us, Azrah ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Follow up between Hajj and Umrah, for they remove sins as the bellows remove the dross of iron."""
"11226","11197 - al-Hasan ibn Abbas al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim ibn Marzuq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from Layth, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man fought in the path of Allah hopefully until he is killed, is he in Paradise? He said: ""Yes."" When he turned away he called him: ""Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: Unless he has debt upon him."""
"11227","11198 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Amr ibn Hisham Abu Umayyah al-Harrani narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taraifi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Religion is sincere advice."" It was said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""To Allah, His Book, His Prophet, the leaders of the Muslims and their common folk."""
"11228","11199 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ayyub al-Wazzan narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibn Thawban, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Whoever fasts a day of Ramadan hopefully, his fasting shall be for him such that if the people of the world gathered from when the world began until it ends, it would suffice them in food and drink; he seeks nothing of that from the people of Paradise."""
"11229","11200 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: My father is an old man unable to perform Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: ""Yes. Tell me, if he had a debt and you paid it on his behalf, would it not suffice for him? This is like that."""
"11230","11201 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Muhammad al-Mubaraki narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Nasibi, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Treat goats well with good, for it is delicate wealth, and it is in Paradise, and the most beloved wealth to Allah is sheep, and upon you is whiteness, for Allah created Paradise white, so let your living wear it and shroud your dead in it, and indeed the blood of a white sheep is greater with Allah than the blood of the two black ones."""
"11231","11202 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Mihran, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a fistula and it flows from me. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""When you perform ablution from your horn to your foot, no ablution is due upon you."""
"11232","11203 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl ibn Muhammad al-Askari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abu Jamilah al-Fadl ibn Salih narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent Budayl ibn Warqa at Mina, who called out: ""These are days of eating and drinking, so do not fast them."""
"11233","11204 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Warqa ibn Amr narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I poured ablution water for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: ""O Allah, grant him understanding in religion and teach him interpretation."""
"11234","11205 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stayed in Makkah thirteen years, and died when he was sixty-three years old."
"11235","11206 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted the menstruating woman to depart before circumambulating if she had already circumambulated."
"11236","11207 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Najjar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Fayyad ibn Muhammad al-Raqqi narrated to us, Marwan al-Ghifari narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by the grave of Musa, peace be upon him, while he was praying in his grave."
"11237","11208 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Umayyah Amr ibn Hisham al-Harrani narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ali ibn Urwah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata and Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had a sword whose hilt was of silver and whose pommel was of silver, and it was called Dhu al-Faqar, and he had a bow called al-Sadad, and he had a quiver called al-Jam, and he had armor decorated with brass called Dhat al-Fudul, and he had a spear called al-Nabaa, and he had a shield called al-Dhaqan, and he had a white buckler called al-Mujaz, and he had a black horse called al-Sakb, and he had a saddle called al-Daj, and he had a white mule called Duldul, and he had a she-camel called al-Qaswa, and he had a donkey called Yafur, and he had a carpet called al-Kurr, and he had a staff called al-Namir, and he had a water-skin called al-Sadir, and he had a mirror called al-Mudillah, and he had scissors called al-Jami, and he had a shawhat-wood staff called al-Mushawwiq."
"11238","11209 - Ahmad ibn Zakariyya Shadhan al-Basri narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Ali al-Qurashi, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Jabir ibn Abdullah came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a quince brought from Taif, and handed it to him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""It removes the heaviness of the chest and clears the heart."""
"11239","11210 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubadah ibn Ziyad al-Asadi narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Ali ibn Urwah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Visiting the sick the first day is Sunnah, and after that is voluntary."
"11240","11211 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It was written upon them that ten shall not flee from two hundred, then He lightened from them, saying: {Now Allah has lightened for you, and He knows there is weakness among you}, the verse, so it was written: that a hundred shall not flee from two hundred."
"11241","11212 - Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I was among those the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent ahead from Muzdalifah to Mina with the dependents."
"11242","11213 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Ukaz and Majannah and Dhu al-Majaz were markets in the pre-Islamic age. When Islam came they felt scrupulous, so Allah Almighty revealed: {There is no blame upon you for seeking bounty from your Lord}, in the seasons of Hajj."
"11243","11214 - Abdullah ibn Musa ibn Abi Uthman al-Anmati narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Ulayy narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata and Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: ""Whoever looks at a gap in a row, let him cover it himself; if he does not do so and a passer passes over him, let him tread upon his neck, for he has no sanctity."""
"11244","11215 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Qawwas narrated to us, Abd al-Majid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Ibn Abbas: that the mockers: Buqayyah ibn al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah - the text as such - and Abu Zamah, and he is al-Aswad ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth, and al-As ibn Wail, he said: All of them were killed at Badr by death or disease, and al-Harith ibn Qays, and he is of the Hayatil."
"11245","11216 - Ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Abu Muhammad al-Jazari, and he is Hamzah al-Nasibi, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Whoever aids falsehood to refute a truth thereby, he is absolved of the protection of Allah and His Messenger. Whoever walks to the authority of Allah to humiliate him, Allah humiliates him along with what He stores for him of disgrace on the Day of Resurrection. The authority of Allah is the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Prophet. Whoever is entrusted with any affair of the Muslim rulers and employs over them a man while knowing there is among them one more deserving and more knowledgeable of the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger, he has betrayed Allah, His Messenger, and all the believers. Whoever neglects the needs of people, Allah will not look into his need until he fulfills their needs and delivers their dues. Whoever eats a dirham of usury, it is thirty-three adulteries. Whoever whose flesh grows from unlawful earnings, the Fire is more deserving of him."""
"11246","11217 - Abdan narrated to us, Ishaq ibn al-Dayf narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: While the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was eating a bone with meat, the caller to prayer came, so he put it down, stood for prayer, and did not touch water."
"11247","11218 - Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Amiri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Ibn Abbas said: It is but a place where the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, camped, meaning al-Abtah."
"11248","11219 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Hasan ibn Salih, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, hastened in the Umrah only because of the polytheists."
"11249","11220 - al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb al-Misri narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Bishr al-Kufi narrated to us, Jami ibn Amr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: ""No one is given charge of an office but well-being is spread for him; if he accepts it, it is completed for him, and if he betrays it, there is opened for him what he has no strength for."" I said to Ibn Abbas: What is betraying it? He said: Seeking slips and faults."
"11250","11221 - Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: We used to recognize the departure of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, by his saying: {Glory be to your Lord, the Lord of might, above what they describe, and peace upon the messengers, and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds}."
"11251","11222 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ali ibn Maymun al-Raqqi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Maslamah, meaning Ibn Ali, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when the first fruits were brought to him, would place them upon his eyes, then say: ""O Allah, as You have fed us its first, feed us its last,"" then he would order it for the newborn of his family."
"11252","Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah from Ibn Abbas. 11223 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf and Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh, the two Egyptians, narrated to us, they said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me, he said: I wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about two women who used to stitch leather; one of them went out claiming her companion struck her with an awl, and the other denied. Ibn Abbas wrote to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged that the oath is upon the one claimed against, and had people been given their claims, people would claim the wealth and blood of people; but call her and recite to her: {Indeed, those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price, they shall have no share in the Hereafter}. He said: So I did, and she confessed, and that reached him and he was pleased with it."
"11253","11224 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Had people been given by their claims, men would claim the wealth and blood of men, but the oath is upon the one claimed against."""
"11254","11225 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Khayyat narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj and Uthman ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Had people been given by their claims, men would claim the wealth and blood of a people."""
"11255","11226 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abu Amir al-Khazzaz, Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to drink honey at Sawdah's, then enter upon Aishah, and she said: I smell an odor from you. Then he entered upon Hafsah, and she said: I smell an odor from you. He said: ""I think it is from a drink I drank at Sawdah's; by Allah I shall not drink it,"" so this verse was revealed: {O Prophet, why do you prohibit what Allah has made lawful for you}."
"11256","11227 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Abu Zufar Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar narrated to us, Musa ibn Khalaf al-Ammi narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The dawn prayer was established, so I stood to pray the two rakahs before dawn, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took my hand and pulled me, saying: ""Do you pray dawn four?"""
"11257","11228 - al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Tawbah al-Qazwini narrated to us, Affan ibn Sayyar narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Indeed my ummah will drink wine in the last times, calling it by other than its name."""
"11258","11229 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Karim al-Zafarani al-Askari and Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Yazid, brother of Rustah, narrated to us, Yaqub Abu Umar Sahib al-Harawi narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to travel from Madinah to Makkah fearing none but Allah, praying two rakahs, two rakahs."
"11259","11230 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Mulayki narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""How can an ummah be sanctified in which the weak cannot take from the strong?"""
"11260","11231 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Malik al-Asbahani narrated to us, Salih ibn Mismar narrated to us, Man ibn Isa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Mulayki narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""All of Arafah is a standing place, but rise above the valley of Uranah; and all of Muzdalifah is a standing place, and rise above the valley of Muhassir."""
"11261","11232 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abdullah al-Mawsili narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us (h), and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Man ibn Isa narrated to us, they both said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Mulayki narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Two supplications between which and Allah there is no veil: the supplication of the wronged, and the supplication of a man for his brother in his absence."""
"11262","11233 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Muammal narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrating from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in the Kabah while Bilal and al-Fadl were at the door. Bilal said: ""He prostrated,"" and al-Fadl said: ""He bowed."""
"11263","11234 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Man ibn Isa ibn Malik narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Muammal narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Take it, O Banu Talhah, eternally everlasting; none shall take it from you but a wrongdoer"" - meaning the custodianship of the Kabah."
"11264","11235 - Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Man ibn Isa narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Muammal, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, continued the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"11265","11236 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Muammal narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Had I been invited to a trotter I would answer."""
"11266","11237 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Muammal narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed the people with his back to the Kabah, between the Stone and the Door."
"11267","11238 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""As though I look at a black bow-legged man uprooting it stone by stone"" - meaning the Kabah."
"11268","11239 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us (h), and Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abu Mashar al-Barra narrated to us (h), and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Harun ibn Muslim narrated to us, all of them from Abdullah ibn al-Akhnas, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""He is not of us who does not chant the Quran."""
"11269","11240 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning this verse: {Except the oppressed among men, women, and children who cannot devise a plan nor are directed to a way}, he said: ""I and my mother were among those Allah excused."""
"11270","11241 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us (h), and Abu Shuayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, they said: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out of the privy, and food was brought near to him. They said: Shall we bring you ablution water? He said: ""I was only commanded with ablution when I stand for prayer."""
"11271","11242 - al-Hasan ibn Alawayh al-Qattan narrated to us, Ismail ibn Isa al-Attar narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Bishr Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Indeed Allah calls people on the Day of Resurrection by their names, as a cover from Him over His servants. As for at the Sirat, Allah Almighty gives every believing man a light and every believing woman a light, and every hypocrite a light. When they are level upon the Sirat, Allah strips the light of the hypocrites, men and women. The hypocrites say: {Wait for us that we may borrow from your light}, and the believers say: {Our Lord, perfect for us our light}. At that time no one remembers anyone."""
"11272","11243 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mualla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abu Shihab al-Hannat narrated to us, Isa ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: ""O boy, guard Allah and He will guard you; guard Allah and you will find Him before you. Know Allah in ease and He will know you in hardship. Know that what befell you could not have missed you, and what missed you could not have befallen you. Know that if creatures gathered to give you something Allah did not will to give you, they could not, or to divert from you something He willed to befall you, they could not. When you ask, ask Allah; when you seek help, seek help from Allah. Know that victory is with patience, relief is with distress, and with hardship is ease. Know that the pen has run with what is to be."""
"11273","11244 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""The partner is a preemptor, and preemption is in everything."""
"11274","11245 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Aswad, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {Until when the messengers despaired and thought they had been denied}, he said: ""They were humans, so they weakened and thought they had been forsaken."" And he read: {Until the messenger says}."
"11275","11246 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar, Abd al-Razzaq said: And I know al-Thawri only narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Aswad, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: ""The sign between us and the hypocrites is that they do not drink their fill of Zamzam."""
"11276","11247 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: It was said to Ibn Abbas: Muawiyah prayed witr with one rakah. He said: ""Leave us from Muawiyah, for he accompanied the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."""
"11277","11248 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd al-Laythi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Allah sends down every day one hundred twenty mercies: sixty of them for those circumambulating, forty for those secluding around the House, and twenty for those looking at the House."""
"11278","11249 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Harithi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""My Hawd is a month's journey, its corners equal, its cups as many as the stars of the sky; its water whiter than snow, sweeter than honey, more fragrant than musk. Whoever drinks a drink from it shall never thirst after it."""
"11279","11250 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr al-Bajali narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah saying: I heard Ibn Abbas: that al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah made food for Quraysh, and when they ate he said: What do you say about this man? Some said: A magician; some said: Not a magician; some said: A soothsayer; some said: Not a soothsayer; some said: A poet; some said: Not a poet; some said: Inherited magic. Their opinion united that it is inherited magic. That reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he grieved, covered his head, and wrapped himself, so Allah revealed: {O you wrapped up. Arise and warn. And your Lord magnify. And your garments purify} {And defilement shun. And do not confer favor to acquire more. And for your Lord be patient}."
"11280","11251 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah and Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered a garden of some of the Ansar and took of the ripe dates eating while walking, and I was with him. He turned to me and said: ""O Ibn Abbas, do not eat with two fingers, for it is the eating of Satan, and eat with three fingers."""
"11281","Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid from Ibn Abbas. 11252 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: I did not know the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seeking the fast of a day, seeking its virtue over others, except this day, the day of Ashura, or the month of Ramadan."
"11282","11252 / 2 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Ibn Abbas, raising it, he said: ""No day has virtue over a day except the month of Ramadan and Ashura."""
"11283","11253 - Yusuf al-Qadi and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""No day has virtue over a day in fasting except the month of Ramadan and the day of Ashura."""
"11284","11254 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari, and Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, they said: Ahmad ibn Ubayd ibn Nistas al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I did not see the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prefer a day over a day except the day of Ashura."
"11285","11255 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Allaf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Yahya ibn Kathir, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not seek the virtue of a day over a day after Ramadan except the day of Ashura."
"11286","11256 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ali ibn Harun al-Zayni narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not fast a day seeking its virtue over a day after Ramadan except the day of Ashura."
"11287","11257 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, similar to it."
"11288","11258 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Dawud ibn Mihran al-Dabbagh narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a sa."
"11289","11259 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would sprinkle water upon his family on the night of twenty-third."
"11290","11260 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I was among those the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent ahead of the weak of his family from Muzdalifah to Mina."
"11291","11261 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us (h), and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me ahead among the weak or among the baggage from Jam by night."
"11292","11262 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Khunays al-Makki narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said to me: Your grandfather Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to me that he heard Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, saying: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw myself in this night in what the sleeper sees, as though I pray by a tree, and as though I recited Surah al-Sajdah and prostrated, and I saw the tree as though it prostrated with my prostration, and as though I hear it saying: O Allah, write for me thereby a reward with You, remove thereby a burden from me, make it for me a store with You, and accept from me as You accepted from Your servant Dawud. Ibn Abbas said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited al-Sajdah, and I heard him saying in his prostration as the man had told him of the tree's saying."
"11293","Abu al-Minhal from Ibn Abbas. 11263 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Abdullah ibn Kathir, from Abu al-Minhal, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Madinah while they were advancing payment for fruit for a year, two years, and three; so he said: ""Whoever advances payment, let him advance in a known measure and known weight to a known term."""
"11294","11264 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Abdullah ibn Kathir, from Abu al-Minhal, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Madinah while they were advancing payment for fruit for two years and three; so he said: ""Whoever advances payment, let him advance in a known measure and known weight to a known term."""
"11295","11265 - Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mamar, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Abdullah ibn Kathir, from Abu al-Minhal, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"11296","11266 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us (h), and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, they said: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Abu al-Minhal, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It was mentioned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Jews fast the day of Ashura, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""If we live, we shall differ from them and fast the ninth day."""
"11297","Umar ibn Ata ibn Abi al-Khuwar from Ibn Abbas. 11267 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Umar ibn Ata ibn Abi al-Khuwar informed me, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: While the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was eating a bone with meat, the caller to prayer came to him, so he put it down, then stood for prayer and did not touch water."
"11298","Humayd al-Damri from Ibn Abbas. 11268 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Humayd al-Damri, that he asked Ibn Abbas, saying: I travel, shall I shorten prayer in travel? Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: It is not shortening, but it is its completion and the Sunnah of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out safe fearing none but Allah and prayed two until he returned."
"11299","11269 - Abu Najih from Ibn Abbas. Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Zurah narrated to us, they said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Zufar ibn al-Hudhayl narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never fought a people until he called them."
"11300","11270 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never fought a people except that he called them."
"11301","11271 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never fought a people until he called them."
"11302","Ikrimah ibn Khalid from Ibn Abbas. 11272 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I was in the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood praying at night; I stood at his left, so he took my hand and placed me at his right, then he prayed thirteen rakahs, about {O you wrapped in garments}."
"11303","Maymun al-Makki from Ibn Abbas. 11273 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu Hubayrah, that Maymun al-Makki informed him, that he saw Ibn al-Zubayr praying with people gesturing with his palms when he stood in prayer: when he stood, when he bowed, when he raised his head from bowing, and when he rose. So I went to Ibn Abbas and said: I saw Ibn al-Zubayr praying a prayer I never saw anyone pray, and I described to him this gesturing. Ibn Abbas said: ""If you wish to look at the prayer of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then follow the prayer of Ibn al-Zubayr."""
"11304","Said al-Allaf from Ibn Abbas. 11274 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mualla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, Said, that is al-Allaf, narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Indeed Allah Almighty has pardoned for my ummah mistake, forgetfulness, and what they are compelled to."""
"11305","Talq ibn Habib from Ibn Abbas. 11275 - Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Talq ibn Habib, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Four things: whoever is given them is given the good of this world and the Hereafter: a grateful heart, a remembering tongue, a body patient over tribulation, and a wife who does not seek betrayal against him in herself or his wealth."""
"11306","Rabah Abu Said al-Makki from Ibn Abbas. 11276 - Masud ibn Muhammad al-Ramli Abu al-Jarud narrated to us, Imran ibn Harun al-Ramli narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Amr narrated to me, from Rabah Abu Said al-Makki, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded him to recite in the dawn prayer By the night when it covers, {By the sun and its brightness}."
"11307","Talhah ibn Nafi from Ibn Abbas. 11277 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Samaah al-Ramli narrated to us (h), and Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Balkhi narrated to us, they said: Ayyub ibn Suwayd al-Ramli narrated to us, Utbah ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan Talhah ibn Nafi, Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated to me, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had promised al-Abbas a herd of camels, so he sent me to him, and I spent the night with him, and it was the night of Maymunah bint al-Harith. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood not long; I reclined on the pillow upon which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had reclined. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood, performed ablution thoroughly with little pouring of water, then stood and began prayer. I stood, performed ablution, and stood at his left, so he moved me with his hand, took my ear, and placed me at his right. Maymunah was menstruating, so she stood, performed ablution, then sat behind him remembering Allah."
"11308","Yusuf ibn Mahak from Ibn Abbas. 11278 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubayd al-Iyadi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas, from al-Walid ibn Abdullah, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Whoever learns a branch of the knowledge of stars has learned a branch of magic; whoever increases, increases; whoever increases, increases."""
"11309","Abu al-Zubayr from Ibn Abbas. 11279 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Barbahari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent his women ahead on the night of Jam before the crowding."
"11310","11280 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Abu al-Zubayr informed him that Abdullah ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to send ahead the dependents and the weak to Mina from Muzdalifah."
"11311","11281 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Abu al-Zubayr informed him, that Abdullah ibn al-Abbas used to say: Staying overnight at al-Muhassab is nothing; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only waited there for Aishah until she arrived."
"11312","11282 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Ibrahim ibn Abi Khidash narrated to me, that Ibn Abbas said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in view of the graveyard, while he was on its first road, he pointed with his hand beyond al-Dafirah or al-Zahirah and said: What an excellent graveyard this is. I said to the one informing me: Did he single out the mountain pass? He said: This is how we used to hear that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) singled out the pass facing the House."
"11313","11283 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Amr ibn Kaysan, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, reciting: Darastu, Talawtu; Khasamtu, Jadaltu."
"11314","11284 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated, Hudhayl ibn Bilal narrated, he said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah and Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr narrating from Ibn Abbas, that a Bedouin came to him and asked him for a drink, so he was given nabidh to drink. He said: What is the matter with your brothers, they give honey and milk to drink, while you give nabidh? He said: Indeed there is no miserliness in us, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked us for a drink and we gave him nabidh to drink, so he said: You have done well and beautifully; do so."
"11315","11285 - Ahmad ibn Zakariyya al-Abidi al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him ahead from Muzdalifah among the weak of his family."
"11316","11286 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Qabisah narrated, my father narrated, Fitr narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."
"11317","11287 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated, Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ahead the weak of his family from Jam at night."
"11318","11288 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Musa ibn Ayan narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only did it to show the polytheists his strength; whoever wishes may do it, and whoever wishes may leave it; meaning al-Ramal."
"11319","11289 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Musabbih narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"11320","11290 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated, Abd al-Malik, the transmitter from Ata, narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I guarantee a house in the outskirts of Paradise, and a house in its highest part, and a house in its lowest part, for whoever abandons argumentation though he is right, and abandons lying though joking, and beautifies his character toward people."
"11321","11291 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night in the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up at night, untied the waterskin and performed ablution, then stood for prayer. So I stood and performed ablution, and stood on his left; he took me with his right hand, turned me from behind him, and placed me on his right, and I prayed with him."
"11322","11292 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Arafah with Usamah ibn Zayd behind him as his companion rider; the she-camel swerved with him while he was raising his hands, not exceeding his head in height. Then he proceeded in the same manner to Jam, with al-Fadl as his companion rider, and he continued the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah."
"11323","11293 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, both said: Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated, Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed a single Tawaf for his Hajj and his Umrah."
"11324","11294 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bukhayt narrated, Said ibn Maslamah narrated, from Layth, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That he used to take good omens and did not take bad omens, and he used to love the good name."
"11325","11295 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi, Abdan ibn Ahmad, and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, they said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Walid al-Wassafi, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no household that maintains kinship ties except that Allah showers provision upon them, and they remain under the protection of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"11326","11295/2 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, both said: Ibn al-Asbahani narrated; and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, both said: Yahya ibn Yaman narrated, from al-Minhal ibn Khalifah, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered a grave at night, with a lamp lit for him in it; he took the deceased from the direction of the Qiblah, said Takbir over him four times, and said: May Allah have mercy on you; you were indeed oft-returning to Allah and oft-reciting the Quran."
"11327","11296 - al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, Ismail ibn al-Khalil al-Khazzaz narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It is from the Sunnah that you do not go out on the day of Fitr until you pay the charity, and eat something before you go out."
"11328","11297 - al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi narrated to us, Abu al-Jawza Ahmad ibn Uthman narrated, Abu Dawud narrated, Shubah narrated, from Hajjaj al-Nakhai, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while he was in Ihram."
"11329","11298 - Humayd ibn Abi Makhlad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated, Mamar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated, from Hajjaj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian, and the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"11330","11299 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated; and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, both from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj; Abu Muawiyah added in his narration: With me."
"11331","11300 - Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Umar ibn Shabbah narrated, Musa ibn Ismail narrated, Uthman ibn Tulayq narrated, from al-Amash, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who woke up fasting? Abu Bakr said: I did. He said: Who visited a sick person? Abu Bakr said: I did. He said: Who accompanied a funeral? Abu Bakr said: I did. He said: Whoever combines them in one day will enter Paradise."
"11332","11301 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated, from Layth, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House, said Takbir in its corners, supplicated, then came out and prayed behind the Maqam."
"11333","11302 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated, from Layth, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wants to give his brother his land, let him grant it to him or let him cultivate it, and let him not give it for a third or a quarter share."
"11334","11303 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, from Layth, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while he was in Ihram."
"11335","11304 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Mualla al-Jufi narrated, from Layth, from Mujahid and Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about bachelorhood and said: Shall I not castrate myself? He said: No; he who castrates or gets castrated is not from us; rather fast and leave the hair of your body."
"11336","11305 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Adam al-Missisi narrated, Muhammad ibn Muyassar Abu Sad al-Saghani narrated, from Abu Jafar al-Razi, from Layth, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I would sometimes see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying while donkeys were fighting in front of him."
"11337","11306 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated, Sharik narrated, from Layth, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I stood on the left of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he took my hand, placed me on his right, and wiped over my head."
"11338","11307 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated, Musa ibn Ayan narrated, from Layth, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Permission was granted to the people of the water supply and the people of the Hijabah to spend the nights of Mina at Makkah; meaning the family of Shaybah and the family of al-Abbas."
"11339","11308 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ismah ibn Sulayman al-Khazzaz narrated, Sharik narrated, from Jabir, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought milk on the day of Arafah, so he drank it and gave drink to the one on his right."
"11340","11309 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Abu Ghassan narrated, Sabbah Abu Abdullah al-Farra narrated, from Jabir, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the wailing woman and the woman who listens, and said: Women have no share in the funeral."
"11341","11310 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Said ibn al-Musayyab ibn Sharik narrated, Abu al-Nadr al-Akfani narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Jabir, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire."
"11342","11311 - Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated, he said: I heard my father, Abu Hamzah narrated, from Jabir, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Tamattu in Hajj is the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11343","11312 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated, Abu Hafs Umar ibn Hafs ibn Yazid al-Qurazi narrated to me, from Amr ibn Shimr, from Jabir ibn Yazid, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hatred of Banu Hashim and the Ansar is disbelief, and hatred of the Arabs is hypocrisy."
"11344","11313 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from al-Suddi, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: Or do they envy people for what Allah has given them of His bounty; Ibn Abbas said: We are the people, apart from other people."
"11345","11314 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Black Stone is from the stones of Paradise, and there is nothing of Paradise on earth besides it; it was white like a wild cow, and were it not for what touched it of the filth of Jahiliyyah, no afflicted person would touch it except that he would be healed."
"11346","11315 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The thorns of the Haram are not to be cut, its game is not to be killed, its herbage is not to be uprooted, and its lost property is not lawful except for one who announces it."
"11347","11316 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I found in my father's book, Ibn Abi Layla narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Qunut in the Fajr prayer, supplicating against a people and supplicating for a people."
"11348","11317 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I found in my father's book, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives a gift is more entitled to his gift so long as he is not compensated for it; if he takes back his gift he is like one who vomits and then eats from it."
"11349","11318 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I found in my father's book, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Jalab in Islam."
"11350","11319 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, Khalid narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued to wipe over the two leather socks until Allah took his soul."
"11351","11320 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated, Hafs ibn Abi Dawud narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting and in Ihram, then he fainted, so on that day he forbade people from a fasting person being cupped, out of dislike of weakness."
"11352","11321 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Said ibn Yahya ibn al-Azhar al-Wasiti narrated, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, from Sharik, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about semen that gets on the garment; he said: It is only like spittle or mucus; remove it from it with a rag or with idhkhir."
"11353","11322 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated to me; and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Talhah and his son performed Hajj on their watering camel and left me. He said: O Umm Sulaym, an Umrah in Ramadan suffices in place of a Hajj."
"11354","11323 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated to me; and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, both from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is a very old man who has not performed Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Tell me, if your father had a debt would you settle it? He said: Yes. He said: Then perform Hajj on his behalf."
"11355","11324 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued the Talbiyah in Umrah until he touched the Stone, and continued the Talbiyah in Hajj until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah on the day of sacrifice."
"11356","11325 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, from Sharik, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out from Madinah to Makkah when he conquered it, and that was in Ramadan, and he was fasting; he fasted until he reached Qudayd, then it reached him that the people had been struck by thirst and hardship, so he called for water, drank, and broke the fast; so whoever wished fasted and whoever wished broke the fast."
"11357","11326 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated; and al-Hasan ibn Alawayh al-Qattan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Marwan al-Khallal narrated, both said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to combine the two prayers while traveling: Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha."
"11358","11327 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated, Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: For a boy two Aqiqahs, and for a girl one Aqiqah."
"11359","11328 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Uthman al-Awdi narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik narrated, from his father, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Ikrimah and Ata, from Ibn Abbas: Then he drew near and came down; he said: It is Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who drew near and came down to his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic."
"11360","11329 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated, Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two horned rams, placing his foot on their sides when he wanted to slaughter, and saying: In the name of Allah, from You and for You; O Allah, accept from Muhammad."
"11361","11330 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Burani, judge of al-Hadithah, and al-Hadithah is from Diyar Rabiah, narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Sudai narrated, al-Hakam ibn al-Jarud narrated, Ibn Abi al-Mutayd, the maternal uncle of Ibn Uyaynah, narrated, from his father, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship until his ease, Allah will grant him respite for his sin until his repentance."
"11362","11331 - Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Sawrah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated, he said: My father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Arzami narrated to me, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Food at a wedding for one day is Sunnah, food for two days is bounty, and food for three days is showing off and seeking repute."
"11363","11332 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated, Sallam al-Tawil narrated, from al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sharp temper befalls the best of my Ummah."
"11364","11333 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Marwan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Umar ibn Salih ibn Khayrah narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah narrated, from his father, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held gold and silk while moving it and saying: This is forbidden for the males of my Ummah."
"11365","11334 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Marwan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Umar ibn Salih ibn Khayrah al-Wasiti narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated, from Kuraz, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying sitting with knees drawn up, with the buttons loosened."
"11366","11335 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated, Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated, from Yusuf ibn Maymun, from Kuraz, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah he said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger have forbidden for you wine and its price, and forbidden for you carrion and its price, and forbidden for you pigs, eating them and their price. And he said: Trim the mustaches, leave the beards, and do not walk in the markets except with waist-wrappers upon you; he who acts upon the practice of other than us is not from us."
"11367","11336 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated, Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated, from Yusuf ibn Maymun, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Umar with some of his Companions and said: Are you believers? They fell silent three times, then Umar said at the last of them: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what makes that so? Umar said: We hope for reward from Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Believers, by the Lord of the Kaaba."
"11368","11337 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Talhah ibn Amr informed me, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, seek treatment, for Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has not created a disease except that He has created for it a cure, except al-Sam; and al-Sam is death."
"11369","11338 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated, Abdullah ibn Raja al-Makki narrated, from Talhah ibn Amr, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an excellent condiment vinegar is."
"11370","11339 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu al-Walid and Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, both said: Hammam narrated, he said: I heard Ata saying: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Kaaba, in which were six pillars; he stood at each pillar and supplicated, and did not pray."
"11371","11340 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated; and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu al-Walid and Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, they said: Shubah narrated, from Ayyub, he said: I heard Ata saying: I bear witness regarding Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Abbas said: I bear witness regarding the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he went out on the day of Fitr, prayed two rakahs, then came to the women with Bilal with him; he commanded them to give charity, and they began to throw."
"11372","11341 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Aswad ibn Amir narrated, Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale involving uncertainty."
"11373","11342 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Aswad ibn Amir narrated, from Ayyub ibn Utbah, from Ikrimah and Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while he was in Ihram."
"11374","11343 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak narrated, al-Rabi ibn Badr narrated, al-Nahhas ibn Qahm narrated, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian, two witnesses, and a dower, whether small or large."
"11375","11344 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ayyub, the companion of al-Basri, narrated, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to perform ablution thoroughly."
"11376","11345 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ayyub and Qays ibn Sad, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the last Isha prayer one night until the people slept and woke up, then slept and woke up; then Umar came and said: O Messenger of Allah, the prayer; so they prayed, and he did not mention that they performed ablution."
"11377","11346 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Ibn Aishah narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ayyub and Yunus, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"11378","11347 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Qays ibn Sad, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he raised his head from bowing, would say: O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise filling the heavens and filling the earth, and filling whatever You will of anything after."
"11379","11348 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated; and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated, both said: Muawiyah ibn Abd al-Karim al-Dall narrated, from Qays ibn Sad, he said: Ata was asked about touching the Stone, so he said: Ibn Abbas said: You have only been commanded to circumambulate; if it is easy then touch it. Al-Dall had lost his way on the road to Makkah and died missing; he said: And Mamar ibn Rashid and Salm ibn Abi al-Dhiyyal were lost, and no trace of them was seen."
"11380","11349 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated, Abbad ibn Mansur narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Bilal on a night of wind and rain, so he called out: Pray in your dwellings."
"11381","11350 - al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Missisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about one who shaved before slaughtering, so he said: No harm."
"11382","11351 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Wasiti narrated, Talhah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from Qatadah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the one in Ihram to wear trousers if he does not find a waist-wrapper, and leather socks if he does not find sandals."
"11383","11352 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Imran Abu Bakr, Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to me, he said: Ibn Abbas said to me: Shall I not show you a woman from the people of Paradise? I said: Yes indeed. He said: This black woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I suffer epilepsy and I become uncovered, so supplicate to Allah for me. He said: If you wish you may be patient and Paradise will be yours, and if you wish I will supplicate to Allah to cure you. She said: I will be patient. She said: I become uncovered, so supplicate to Allah that I not become uncovered; so he supplicated for her."
"11384","11353 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated; and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated; and Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, they said: Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I was among those sent ahead with the baggage of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of Jam."
"11385","11354 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, al-Rabi ibn Subayh narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ahead the weak of his family on the night of Muzdalifah, and commanded them not to stone the Jamrah until the sun rises."
"11386","11355 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Nuaym al-Wasiti narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Kathir ibn Shinzhir, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The beginning of hastening only came from the people of the desert; they would stand at the edges of the people with bows and quivers hung upon them, then when they departed they would clatter. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was indeed seen, with the temples of his she-camel almost touching its hump, while he was saying: O people, calmness is incumbent upon you; O people, calmness is incumbent upon you."
"11387","11356 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated; and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, both said: Said ibn Mansur narrated; and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Ahmar al-Naqid al-Basri narrated to us, Talut ibn Abbad narrated, they said: al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Ila of the people of Jahiliyyah was a year and two years; then Allah fixed a time for Ila: whoever's Ila is less than four months is not an Ila. And the wording is that of the narration of Said ibn Mansur."
"11388","11357 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Abdi narrated, Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated; and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated, Ibrahim al-Saigh narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led the people in prayer on the day of Fitr, two rakahs without Adhan or Iqamah, then delivered the sermon after the prayer, then took Bilal by the hand and went to the women and addressed them, then after turning away from them he commanded Bilal to go to them and order them to give charity."
"11389","11358 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Nasai narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated, Awn ibn Mamar narrated, from Ibrahim al-Saigh, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: They waited for the prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque, then they dozed; then we woke up three times, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us, prayed Isha, and said: Were it not that I would burden the people, I would have commanded them to delay this prayer to this hour; so we looked and it was midnight."
"11390","11359 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib narrated to me, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated, from Ibrahim al-Saigh, Ata narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Banu Abd Manaf, if you are entrusted with this authority after me, do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House or prays at whatever hour he wishes, by night or by day."
"11391","11360 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid narrated, from Husayn al-Muallim, from Ata, Ibn Abbas narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send the baggage ahead before dawn; and I was among those sent, meaning from Muzdalifah."
"11392","11361 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, Nafi Abu Hurmuz narrated, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best of the angels, Jibril, peace be upon him; and the best of the prophets, Adam; and the best of the women, Maryam daughter of Imran."
"11393","11362 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, Nafi Abu Hurmuz narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say Takbir seven times over the people of Badr, and five Takbirs over Banu Hashim; then his last prayer was four Takbirs until he left this world."
"11394","11363 - Ibrahim narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, Nafi Abu Hurmuz narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Two Qirats are placed in his scale, each Qirat like Uhud; meaning one who follows the funeral."
"11395","11364 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah narrated to us, Shayban narrated, Nafi Abu Hurmuz narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When midday arrived, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out to one of the gardens of Madinah, where purification had been prepared for him therein; if he had a need he would relieve it, otherwise he would purify himself. Then when the sun declined from the middle of the sky by a sandal-strap's measure, he would stand and pray four rakahs, without Tashahhud between them, saluting at the end of the four. Then he would stand and come to the mosque. Ibn Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this prayer that you pray and we do not pray? Ibn Abbas said: Whoever of my Ummah prays them has enlivened his night for an hour in which the doors of heaven are opened and supplication is answered therein."
"11396","11365 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah narrated to us, Shayban narrated, Nafi Abu Hurmuz narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: al-Abbas came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at an hour at which he would not come to him, so it was said: O Messenger of Allah, this is your uncle at the door. He said: Give him permission, for he has come for a matter. When he entered upon him he said: What has brought you, O my uncle, at this hour, which is not the hour at which you used to come? He said: O son of my brother, I remembered Jahiliyyah and its ignorance, so the world became straitened upon me despite its vastness, and I said: Who will relieve me? So I knew that none would relieve me except Allah, then you. He said: Praise be to Allah who cast this into your heart; and I wished that Abu Talib had taken his share, but Allah does what He wills. He said: Shall I grant you a gift? He said: Yes. He said: Shall I give you? He said: Yes. He said: Shall I grant you a gift? He said: Yes. He said: When there is an hour in which prayer is performed, neither after Asr nor after sunrise, in between that, then perfect your purification, then stand before Allah and recite the Opening of the Book and a Surah; if you wish make it from the beginning of the Mufassal. When you finish the Surah, say: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, fifteen times. When you bow, say that ten times; when you raise your head, say that ten times."
"11397","11366 - Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, Nafi Abu Hurmuz narrated, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was being cupped on Tuesday, so I said: Do you get cupped on this day? He said: Yes; whoever among you coincides with Tuesday, the night of the seventeenth past of the month, let him not pass it until he gets cupped; so get cupped."
"11398","11367 - Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, Nafi Abu Hurmuz narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I did not pass by any assembly of angels except that they commanded me with cupping."
"11399","11368 - Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, Nafi Abu Hurmuz narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Iblis has rebels among the devils to whom he says: Upon you be the pilgrims and the strivers, so lead them astray from the path."
"11400","11369 - Abu Abd al-Malik Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, Sadan ibn Yahya narrated, Nafi, freedman of Yusuf al-Sulami, narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The key of prayer is purification, its inviolability is the Takbir, and its permissibility is the Taslim."
